{"traceId":"70b7ee512dbfe2cadb5e130cdabda658","spans":{"21eb3840532d8b50":{"spanId":"21eb3840532d8b50","traceId":"70b7ee512dbfe2cadb5e130cdabda658","parentSpanId":"600f22c238525756","startTime":1753403902557,"endTime":1753403946324.696,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"openai/o3","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{openai/o3,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure solution using any tech stack that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of the user's personal machine command line. Using the command line, you can create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, writing code, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and deploying applications.\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team (tokens) and in the context of the user (budget, cloud services, etc.). You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. **Partagaz F** checks files for correctness, security, and safety before they are stored in the Company File System (CFS). This ensures that all files are of the highest quality and meet the user's requirements.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Initial engagement: introduce myself as the user's Chief of Staff and discover their immediate need so we can begin planning and allocating resources appropriately.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Hello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. What can I create for you today?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:33:27.818Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. What can I create for you today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:33:27.818Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Gather essential details about hosting, user management, content, and preferences so we can propose an appropriate architecture, design, and implementation plan that matches the User’s technical comfort level and budget.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1. Do you already own a domain name for the HOA website, or would you like us to secure and configure one for you?\\\",\\n    \\\"2. Do you have a preferred hosting provider (e.g., GoDaddy, Squarespace, AWS) or would you like us to recommend an economical, secure option and manage it for you?\\\",\\n    \\\"3. Approximately how many residents will need login accounts, and do you prefer self-registration (e.g., residents sign up with a code) or administrator-created accounts?\\\",\\n    \\\"4. What kinds of files (PDF, Word, images, etc.) and approximate sizes will you upload for meeting minutes and financial reports?\\\",\\n    \\\"5. Will the Dues page simply list information, or would you like to accept online payments (credit card, ACH) through the site?\\\",\\n    \\\"6. Do you already have branding assets (logo, colors, photos) or would you like us to design/provide them?\\\",\\n    \\\"7. Would you like residents to receive email notifications/newsletters when new items are posted to News & Events?\\\",\\n    \\\"8. Do you have a target launch date or budget range in mind so we can tailor the solution accordingly?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify2###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:35:29.533Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1. Do you already own a domain name for the HOA website, or would you like us to secure and configure one for you?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2. Do you have a preferred hosting provider (e.g., GoDaddy, Squarespace, AWS) or would you like us to recommend an economical, secure option and manage it for you?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3. Approximately how many residents will need login accounts, and do you prefer self-registration (e.g., residents sign up with a code) or administrator-created accounts?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100, yes self-registration\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4. What kinds of files (PDF, Word, images, etc.) and approximate sizes will you upload for meeting minutes and financial reports?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"PDF files no more than 10 pages\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5. Will the Dues page simply list information, or would you like to accept online payments (credit card, ACH) through the site?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Simply list info\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"6. Do you already have branding assets (logo, colors, photos) or would you like us to design/provide them?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"7. Would you like residents to receive email notifications/newsletters when new items are posted to News & Events?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"8. Do you have a target launch date or budget range in mind so we can tailor the solution accordingly?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No, although as low as possible please\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:35:29.533Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###recruit-infra###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We need a high-level leader to plan low-cost, secure hosting, configure the existing domain (dunbaroakshoa.com), set up WordPress, SSL, backups, and lay out a deterministic infrastructure plan that other teams can rely on.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Infrastructure & Deployment\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"You are responsible for selecting economical hosting, configuring DNS/SSL, installing WordPress, and documenting an infrastructure DEP that other teams can follow.\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-infra###\\n###recruit-wp###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We require a senior specialist to architect the WordPress setup: create pages, select and configure plugins for authentication, self-registration, and protected content, ensuring usability for a non-technical HOA admin.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of CMS Implementation\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"You will design the WordPress information architecture, choose plugins (login, membership, contact form), define user roles, and produce a deterministic plan for implementing pages and protected sections.\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-wp###\\n###recruit-design###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"A dedicated design leader is needed to craft branding (logo, colors) and customize a responsive WordPress theme so the site looks polished yet remains easy to maintain.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Design & Branding\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Create a simple, professional visual identity, pick or modify a free theme, and document styling choices so non-technical admins can maintain consistency.\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-design###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:36:36.971Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-infra\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent F (4) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-wp\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Motti (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-design\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent D (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:36:36.971Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###order-infra###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Infrastructure & Deployment. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Select a low-cost, secure hosting approach suitable for ~100 WordPress users (e.g., reputable shared WP host or AWS Lightsail WP image) and compare at least two options with pricing, recommending one.\\\\n2. Detail exact setup steps: purchasing or linking the existing domain dunbaroakshoa.com, DNS changes, SSL (Let’s Encrypt or host-provided), automatic backups, and uptime monitoring—all with commands or provider UI clicks spelled out deterministically.\\\\n3. Include WordPress installation steps, staging ↔ production workflow, and basic hardening (firewall, limited login attempts, automatic updates).\\\\n4. Provide estimated recurring and one-time costs, and note any free-tier limits.\\\\n5. Specify any dependencies or information you need from the CMS & Design directors.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID INFRA_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"F\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"INFRA_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-infra###\\n###order-cms###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for CMS Implementation. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Define the WordPress information architecture: Home, Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings (protected), News & Events (protected).\\\\n2. Recommend and justify specific free/low-cost plugins for: a) resident self-registration (~100 users) with admin approval code; b) content protection/membership; c) simple page builder or block pattern for non-technical updates; d) contact form; e) PDF file management.\\\\n3. Outline exact configuration steps for each plugin, user-role definitions, and sample workflow for the HOA admin to upload/update protected content and news posts without coding.\\\\n4. Address basic security (CAPTCHA, limited login attempts) and privacy (no unnecessary data collection).\\\\n5. List any settings or theme hooks the Design director must accommodate and any hosting prerequisites from Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"Motti\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-cms###\\n###order-design###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Design & Branding. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Propose a simple, professional visual identity: color palette (3–5 colors), typography (Google Fonts), and a logo concept appropriate for Dunbar Oaks HOA.\\\\n2. Select a free, responsive WordPress theme that supports the CMS director’s plugin choices; outline any child-theme or Customizer tweaks needed.\\\\n3. Provide step-by-step instructions for applying the branding in WordPress (logo upload, colors, fonts) and for customizing key page layouts (header, footer, navigation) without coding where possible.\\\\n4. Export a one-page style guide (PDF or image) for future reference.\\\\n5. Note any asset sizes/formats required from the User (e.g., neighborhood photo) and any technical hooks that Infrastructure/CMS teams must enable.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID DESIGN_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"D\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DESIGN_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-design###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Malformed Call Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis automated message is to inform you that you that one or more of your attached system calls was not in the correct format.\\\\n\\\\nThe system program can only accept calls in the correct format. Please correct your call(s) and resubmit.\\\\n\\\\nSee below for the specific errors generated by your calls.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nCall ID order-infra failed inspection: Call order-infra of type ORDER failed inspection: recipient agent ID NaN does not exist.\\\"\\n}\\n###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###order-infra###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Infrastructure & Deployment. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Select a low-cost, secure hosting approach suitable for ~100 WordPress users (e.g., reputable shared WP host or AWS Lightsail WP image) and compare at least two options with pricing, recommending one.\\\\n2. Detail exact setup steps: purchasing or linking the existing domain dunbaroakshoa.com, DNS changes, SSL (Let’s Encrypt or host-provided), automatic backups, and uptime monitoring—spell out every command or provider UI action deterministically.\\\\n3. Include WordPress installation steps, staging ↔ production workflow, and basic hardening (firewall, limited login attempts, automatic updates).\\\\n4. Provide estimated recurring and one-time costs, and note any free-tier limits.\\\\n5. Specify any dependencies or information you need from the CMS & Design directors.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID INFRA_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"4\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"INFRA_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-infra###\\n###order-cms###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for CMS Implementation. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Define the WordPress information architecture: Home, Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings (protected), News & Events (protected).\\\\n2. Recommend and justify specific free/low-cost plugins for: a) resident self-registration (~100 users) with admin approval code; b) content protection/membership; c) simple page builder or block pattern for non-technical updates; d) contact form; e) PDF file management.\\\\n3. Outline exact configuration steps for each plugin, user-role definitions, and sample workflow for the HOA admin to upload/update protected content and news posts without coding.\\\\n4. Address basic security (CAPTCHA, limited login attempts) and privacy (no unnecessary data collection).\\\\n5. List any settings or theme hooks the Design director must accommodate and any hosting prerequisites from Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"3\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-cms###\\n###order-design###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Design & Branding. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Propose a simple, professional visual identity: color palette (3–5 colors), typography (Google Fonts), and a logo concept appropriate for Dunbar Oaks HOA.\\\\n2. Select a free, responsive WordPress theme that supports the CMS director’s plugin choices; outline any child-theme or Customizer tweaks needed.\\\\n3. Provide step-by-step instructions for applying the branding in WordPress (logo upload, colors, fonts) and for customizing key page layouts (header, footer, navigation) without coding where possible.\\\\n4. Export a one-page style guide (PDF or image) for future reference.\\\\n5. Note any asset sizes/formats required from the User (e.g., neighborhood photo) and any technical hooks that Infrastructure/CMS teams must enable.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID DESIGN_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"2\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DESIGN_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-design###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:38:22.513Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-infra\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order INFRA_PLAN_V1 from agent 4: INFRASTRUCTURE & DEPLOYMENT – DETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP)\\\\\\\\nSequence ID: INFRA_PLAN_V1\\\\\\\\nResponsible Agent: Director-rank (Hearts)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nA. OPTION COMPARISON & RECOMMENDATION\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nOption 1 – AWS Lightsail WordPress Blueprint\\\\\\\\n  • Instance (Plan) – 1 vCPU / 1 GB RAM / 40 GB SSD\\\\\\\\n  • Price – $5.00 USD / month flat (first month free)  \\\\\\\\n  • Data transfer – 2 TB included; overage $0.09/GB  \\\\\\\\n  • Snapshot backup – manual or scheduled, $0.05 / GB-month (≈$2 / mo for 40 GB)\\\\\\\\n  • Integrated DNS zones (free for first 3 zones), bundled static IP, built-in HTTPS via Let’s Encrypt, and one-click scaling.\\\\\\\\n  • Root SSH & WP admin access, security groups (firewall) configurable, AWS CLI available for IaC.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nOption 2 – Namecheap “EasyWP Turbo” Managed WordPress\\\\\\\\n  • Price – $4.88 USD / mo (annual billing) or $8.88 / mo monthly  \\\\\\\\n  • Visitors – up to 200 k/month, 1.5 CPU & 768 MB RAM burstable  \\\\\\\\n  • Storage – 25 GB SSD  \\\\\\\\n  • Free CDN and SSL (Sectigo)  \\\\\\\\n  • Backups – daily automatic (free), on-demand $2.00 each  \\\\\\\\n  • Limited root / plugin control; no AWS-grade scalability.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRecommendation: AWS Lightsail WordPress Blueprint.\\\\\\\\n  – Similar pricing; stronger scalability path (upgrade instance or migrate to EC2/EKS), granular firewall rules, snapshot-level backups, CLI automation, and easier multi-environment cloning.  \\\\\\\\n  – Includes 1 static IP & free monthly cost credits for first month.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nB. HIGH-LEVEL DEPENDENCIES\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nD1. Registrar credentials for dunbaroakshoa.com (assumed currently at GoDaddy).  \\\\\\\\nD2. AWS root or IAM user with Lightsail + Route 53 + Certificate Manager permissions.  \\\\\\\\nD3. CMS/Design team to supply: (a) chosen WP theme & plugins list, (b) branding assets, (c) staging content requirements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nC. STEP-BY-STEP EXECUTION – FULLY DETERMINISTIC\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nNOTE: Steps are numbered; execute sequentially. Commands prefixed “$” are run from an authorized local shell with AWS CLI v2 configured (profile «do-hoa»). UI clicks use exact menu paths.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 0. Local Workstation Prep ——\\\\\\\\n0.1  Install AWS CLI v2 & Lightsailctl plugin (if not present):\\\\\\\\n     $ curl \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -o awscliv2.zip\\\\\\\\n     $ unzip awscliv2.zip && sudo ./aws/install\\\\\\\\n     $ pip install awscli-plugin-lightsail\\\\\\\\n0.2  Configure profile with least-privilege IAM creds:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws configure --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n     (enter Access Key, Secret, us-east-1, json)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 1. Networking & DNS ——\\\\\\\\n1.1  Create Route 53 public hosted zone (if DNS will migrate):\\\\\\\\n     $ aws route53 create-hosted-zone --name dunbaroakshoa.com --caller-reference $(date +%s) --profile do-hoa > /tmp/zone.json\\\\\\\\n     Record HostedZoneId = $(jq -r '.HostedZone.Id' /tmp/zone.json)\\\\\\\\n1.2  If keeping registrar DNS, skip 1.1 and obtain existing control panel.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 2. Lightsail Instance Provisioning ——\\\\\\\\n2.1  Allocate static IP:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail allocate-static-ip --static-ip-name do-prod-ip --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n2.2  Create production instance:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail create-instances \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --instance-names do-prod-wp \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --availability-zone us-east-1a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --blueprint-id wordpress \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --bundle-id micro_2_0 (represents 1GB/40GB) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --user-data file://disable_ping.sh \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n2.3  Attach static IP:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail attach-static-ip --static-ip-name do-prod-ip --instance-name do-prod-wp --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n2.4  Repeat 2.1-2.3 with names do-stage-ip / do-stage-wp for staging environment.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 3. DNS Records ——\\\\\\\\n3.1  Create A record \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"@\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" → static prod IP & CNAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"www\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" → dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\n     If Route 53:\\\\\\\\n     $ cat > /tmp/rr.json <<EOF\\\\\\\\n     {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Comment\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A + CNAME\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Changes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"UPSERT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecordSet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TTL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":300,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecords\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"<PROD_IP>\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"UPSERT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecordSet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"www.dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CNAME\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TTL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":300,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecords\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}}]}\\\\\\\\n     EOF\\\\\\\\n     $ aws route53 change-resource-record-sets --hosted-zone-id $HostedZoneId --change-batch file:///tmp/rr.json --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n3.2  At registrar, replace nameservers with those from Route 53 OR create A/CNAME records if staying.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 4. SSL/TLS Certificates ——\\\\\\\\n4.1  In Lightsail console → Networking → HTTPS → “Enable HTTPS” → Let’s Encrypt → pick dunbaroakshoa.com + www. System auto-installs certbot & cron renewals. Deterministic via CLI:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail create-certificate --certificate-name do-cert --domain-name dunbaroakshoa.com --subject-alternative-names www.dunbaroakshoa.com --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail attach-certificate-to-distribution ... (Lightsail auto-distribution optional)\\\\\\\\n4.2  Verify `https://dunbaroakshoa.com` green padlock in browser.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 5. WordPress Initialisation ——\\\\\\\\n5.1  Retrieve WP admin password:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail get-instance --instance-name do-prod-wp --profile do-hoa | jq -r '.instance.username'\\\\\\\\n     ssh bitnami@<PROD_IP>\\\\\\\\n     $ cat ~/bitnami_application_password\\\\\\\\n5.2  Log into `https://dunbaroakshoa.com/wp-admin`, change password, set site title.\\\\\\\\n5.3  Install plugin “Limit Login Attempts Reloaded” (Security → Add New → search).\\\\\\\\n5.4  Enable automatic WP core/theme/plugin updates: Dashboard → Updates → “Enable automatic”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 6. Staging ↔ Production Workflow ——\\\\\\\\n6.1  Stage site lives on do-stage-wp, IP e.g., 3.3.3.3, DNS: staging.dunbaroakshoa.com (A record).\\\\\\\\n6.2  Deploy Pipeline (manual deterministic):\\\\\\\\n     a) WP Plugin “All-in-One WP Migration” installed on both envs.  \\\\\\\\n     b) On staging: Export → File.  \\\\\\\\n     c) scp file to local or directly import on production.  \\\\\\\\n     (Future: Implement Lightsail Snapshots & AWS CodePipeline for blue-green; out of scope but feasible.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 7. Backups ——\\\\\\\\n7.1  Automated snapshot schedule (daily, retain 7):\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail put-instance-public-ports --instance-name do-prod-wp --port-infos file://ports.json --profile do-hoa  # (allows snapshot API)\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail create-auto-snapshot-add-on --instance-name do-prod-wp --add-on-type AutoSnapshot --status Enabled --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n7.2  Confirm: $ aws lightsail get-auto-snapshots --instance-name do-prod-wp --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n7.3  Repeat for staging.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 8. Uptime Monitoring ——\\\\\\\\n8.1  Enable Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics (free for 100 canaries-runs per month in Free Tier):\\\\\\\\n     $ aws synthetics create-canary --name do-home-canary --code S3Bucket=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"synthetics-bucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",S3Key=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ping.zip\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --execution-role-arn <ROLE> --schedule \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rate(5 minutes)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --run-config timeoutInSeconds=60 --artifact-s3-location s3://synthetics-artifacts/ --runtime-version syn-nodejs-puppeteer-3.4 --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n8.2  Alarm: 2 consecutive failures triggers SNS → email admin.\\\\\\\\n     (Alternatively, use free UptimeRobot monitor if AWS budget sensitive.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 9. Firewall Hardening ——\\\\\\\\n9.1  Default Lightsail firewall: Allow 80/tcp, 443/tcp, 22/tcp (SSH) from owner IP only; disable ping.\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail open-instance-public-ports --instance-name do-prod-wp --port-info fromPort=22,toPort=22,protocol=TCP,cidr=<OFFICE_IP>/32 --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n9.2  Disable XML-RPC: WP plugin “Disable XMLRPC-Pingback”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 10. Post-Deployment Validation ——\\\\\\\\n10.1  SSL Labs test score ≥ A.  \\\\\\\\n10.2  Wordfence scan passes; login attempts limited.  \\\\\\\\n10.3  CloudWatch canary status OK.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nD. COST SUMMARY (USD)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nRECURRING\\\\\\\\n  • Lightsail Prod instance: $5.00 / mo\\\\\\\\n  • Lightsail Stage instance: $5.00 / mo (can be stopped when idle to <$1)\\\\\\\\n  • Snapshots (~40 GB each): 2 × $2.00 ≈ $4.00 / mo\\\\\\\\n  • Route 53 Hosted Zone: $0.50 / mo + $0.40 / million queries (negligible)\\\\\\\\n  • CloudWatch Canaries: <$1 in Free Tier (first year) ⇒ then $4.50 / mo if 5-min interval\\\\\\\\nTotal steady-state ≈ $14.50 – $18.00 / month\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nONE-TIME\\\\\\\\n  • Domain transfer (if moving registrars): ~$9.00 (includes 1-year renewal)  \\\\\\\\n  • Initial snapshot storage grows linearly but negligible (<$1) first month\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFREE-TIER / NO-COST ITEMS\\\\\\\\n  • First Lightsail month free  \\\\\\\\n  • Let’s Encrypt SSL  \\\\\\\\n  • Up to 3 Route 53 DNS health checks free for 12 months  \\\\\\\\n  • AWS Free Tier 1 GB snapshot storage  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nE. HAND-OFF ARTIFACTS\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nE1. Generated HostedZoneId and static IPs – to be documented in shared secrets vault.\\\\\\\\nE2. Saved AWS CLI commands log (/var/log/infra-deploy-$(date).log) for audit.\\\\\\\\nE3. CloudFormation template (optional) to codify steps 2-7 – can be produced on request.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nF. NEXT-STE P REQUESTS TO CMS / DESIGN DIRECTORS\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nF1. Confirm choice of theme/plugins so we can pre-install in AMI snapshot.  \\\\\\\\nF2. Supply favicon & logo to complete staging site before production push.  \\\\\\\\nF3. Provide colour palette to configure CDN edge rules for image optimisation (optional).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nEnd of DEP – ready for Partagaz D review.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-cms\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order CMS_PLAN_V1 from agent 3: **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – CMS_PLAN_V1**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nA. HOSTING & BASELINE\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Hosting prerequisites (Infrastructure team)\\\\\\\\n   a. PHP ≥ 8.1, memory_limit ≥ 256 M, max_upload_filesize ≥ 32 M.\\\\\\\\n   b. MariaDB 10.5 / MySQL 8.0, InnoDB default.\\\\\\\\n   c. HTTPS enabled (Let’s Encrypt or other TLS cert) before public launch.\\\\\\\\n   d. Cron jobs allowed (for WP‐Cron replacement if traffic < 1k/day this can stay virtual).\\\\\\\\n   e. SMTP credentials or transactional-mail service (Postmark / SendGrid free tier) for registration emails.\\\\\\\\n   f. File-system write permissions for wp-content and install zip uploads.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Fresh WordPress 6.5.x install in root directory; enforce automatic minor/major core updates:\\\\\\\\n   wp-config.php →\\\\\\\\n   define('WP_AUTO_UPDATE_CORE','minor');\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Theme baseline picked by Design director: “Twenty Twenty-Four” **or** “Astra Free”.\\\\\\\\n   • Must support: full-site-editing (FSE) hooks `header`, `footer`, `sidebar` if Astra.\\\\\\\\n   • Keep child-theme blank (style.css, functions.php) reserved for any CSS/JS overrides but *initially empty* to keep DEP deterministic.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nB. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE (IA)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nCreate pages in this exact slug order:\\\\\\\\n1. `/`  → “Home”\\\\\\\\n2. `/contact-us/` → “Contact Us”\\\\\\\\n3. `/bylaws/` → “HOA Bylaws” (public)\\\\\\\\n4. `/schools/` → “Nearby Schools” (public)\\\\\\\\n5. `/dues/` → “Dues” (PROTECTED)\\\\\\\\n6. `/annual-meetings/` → “Annual Meetings” (PROTECTED)\\\\\\\\n7. `/news-events/` → “News & Events” (PROTECTED)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNavigation menu “Main Menu” created and assigned to Theme primary location using identical order.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nC. PLUGIN STACK (all free unless noted)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. User self-registration + manual admin approval + access-code field\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“User Registration – Custom Registration Form, Login and User Profile”** by WP Everest.\\\\\\\\n     – Free tier supports manual approval, custom fields & form shortcodes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Content/membership protection\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Content Control – User Access Restriction”** by Code Atlantic (100 % free, no paywall).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Simple page/block builder for non-technical updates\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Kadence Blocks – Gutenberg Blocks for Page Builder Features”** (free) – adds pre-made block patterns, accordions, tabs; stays inside core editor.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Contact form with CAPTCHA\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“WPForms Lite”** (free) – includes hCaptcha & reCAPTCHA v2/v3 support.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. PDF file management / embed & protection\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“EmbedPress”** (free) – Gutenberg block to embed PDF inline.\\\\\\\\n   • **“Prevent Direct Access – PDA Lite”** (free) – protects PDFs so file URLs respect membership rules.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Security hardening\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Limit Login Attempts Reloaded”** (free).\\\\\\\\n   • (Optional) “WP 2FA” free module if MFA desired later.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Role/Capability management convenience\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Members”** by MemberPress (free) – create Custom Role “Resident”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nD. STEP-BY-STEP CONFIGURATION\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nD1. Global order of operations (deterministic):\\\\\\\\n   1. Complete WP install (A2).\\\\\\\\n   2. Install theme (A3).\\\\\\\\n   3. Install *all* plugins in section C but keep them **deactivated**.\\\\\\\\n   4. Activate plugins sequentially in this exact order to avoid capability conflicts:\\\\\\\\n      a. Members\\\\\\\\n      b. User Registration\\\\\\\\n      c. Content Control\\\\\\\\n      d. Kadence Blocks\\\\\\\\n      e. WPForms Lite\\\\\\\\n      f. EmbedPress\\\\\\\\n      g. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite\\\\\\\\n      h. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\\\\\n   5. Create roles, forms, rules as below.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD2. Members plugin – role definitions\\\\\\\\n   • Create custom role **Resident**.\\\\\\\\n     Capabilities: `read`, `edit_posts` = false, `upload_files` = false. (Leave all others unchecked.)\\\\\\\\n   • (Core) Keep Administrator, Editor defaults.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD3. User Registration plugin – registration form\\\\\\\\n   1. Create new form “Resident Signup”.\\\\\\\\n   2. Add core fields: First Name, Last Name, Email (username), Password.\\\\\\\\n   3. Add custom Text field “Access Code”.\\\\\\\\n      – Field meta-key: `hoa_access_code`.\\\\\\\\n      – Field set as *required*.\\\\\\\\n   4. Enable *Manual Admin Approval* (Settings ▸ General ▸ User Login Option ▸ “Admin Approve”).\\\\\\\\n   5. Form setting ▸ *Enable email confirmation* = OFF (because approval already required).\\\\\\\\n   6. Place validation rule via form *Field Visibility & Logic*:\\\\\\\\n      – If `hoa_access_code` ≠ “NEIGHBOR2024” (example), display error “Invalid HOA code”.\\\\\\\\n   7. Save form; copy generated shortcode `[user_registration_form id=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"XX\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]`.\\\\\\\\n   8. Create WordPress page `/register/` titled “Resident Registration”, paste shortcode.\\\\\\\\n   9. In WP ▸ Settings ▸ General ▸ “Membership – Anyone can register” = **unchecked** (security).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD4. Content Control – protection rules\\\\\\\\n   • Rule 1: Protect Pages `Dues`, `Annual Meetings`, `News & Events`.\\\\\\\\n     – Access condition: Logged-in users with role = Resident OR ≥ Editor.\\\\\\\\n     – Redirect on failure: `/register/` (or custom message page).\\\\\\\\n   • Rule 2: Protect Media Files category “Protected PDFs” (auto-created by PDA Lite) with same role condition.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD5. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite – PDF handling\\\\\\\\n   1. Settings ▸ Permalink Type: “Encrypted URL” (default).\\\\\\\\n   2. Upload PDF → Media Library → toggle “Protect this file”.\\\\\\\\n   3. Copy shortcode `[pda_protected url=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" download=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]` and insert inside protected pages.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD6. WPForms Lite – contact form\\\\\\\\n   1. Create form “HOA Contact”. Fields: Name, Email, Message.\\\\\\\\n   2. Settings ▸ Spam Protection → enable Google reCAPTCHA v3 (site key provided separately by Infrastructure).\\\\\\\\n   3. Notifications → send to `hoaboard@example.com`.\\\\\\\\n   4. Embed form in “Contact Us” page using Gutenberg block.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD7. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\\\\\n   • Settings → Lockout at 4 retries, 30 min lockout, 24 h increase, GDPR consent banner OFF.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD8. Kadence Blocks (non-technical editing enablement)\\\\\\\\n   • Install Starter Templates if Astra theme chosen; else use built-in patterns.\\\\\\\\n   • Provide training doc (outside DEP) listing: Accordion (meeting minutes), Info Box (dues summary), Gallery (events photos).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nE. SAMPLE WORKFLOWS\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Resident onboarding\\\\\\\\n   a. User visits /register/; enters data + HOA access code.\\\\\\\\n   b. Admin receives email “User Registration Requires Approval”.\\\\\\\\n   c. Admin logs in → User Registration ▸ Users → Approve.\\\\\\\\n   d. User receives “Your account is approved” email, logs in, sees protected menu items.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. HOA Admin uploads protected PDF (e.g., Annual Meeting Minutes)\\\\\\\\n   a. Media ▸ Add New → upload PDF → click “Protect this file”.\\\\\\\\n   b. Copy auto-generated shortcode.\\\\\\\\n   c. Edit “Annual Meetings” page (block editor) → add ‘Shortcode’ block → paste.\\\\\\\\n   d. Click Update; file now downloadable only by Residents.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Post News item\\\\\\\\n   a. Posts ▸ Add New → title + content; set Category = “Members Only News”.\\\\\\\\n   b. Content Control rule can also blanket-protect this category if preferred (create Rule 3 referencing category).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nF. SECURITY / PRIVACY CHECKLIST\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n✔ SSL mandatory.\\\\\\\\n✔ Limit Login Attempts active.\\\\\\\\n✔ reCAPTCHA on Contact form.\\\\\\\\n✔ Manual approval prevents spam users.\\\\\\\\n✔ Only essential PII collected (name, email, HOA access code). No DOB, phone, etc.\\\\\\\\n✔ Weekly automated backups via host or UpdraftPlus (free) – schedule to external storage (Google Drive free tier).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nG. DESIGN TEAM HOOKS & NOTES\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Theme must output `wp_nav_menu()` location “primary”.\\\\\\\\n2. Register sidebar “Protected Sidebar” (optional) if theme offers sidebars → may hold quick-links visible only to Residents via `is_user_logged_in()`.\\\\\\\\n3. Ensure CSS for `.pda-protected` shortcode wrapper inherits theme typography.\\\\\\\\n4. If using Astra, keep header builder; add custom menu item CSS class `menu-item-protected` (style to match but hide via `display:none` unauth if plugin flashes). Not needed for FSE theme.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nH. DELIVERABLE SUMMARY\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• Working WordPress site with defined IA, plugins configured, roles created.\\\\\\\\n• No paid licenses required; all plugins on WP.org repo.\\\\\\\\n• Non-technical HOA admins can manage protected documents and news via Gutenberg + Kadence Blocks.\\\\\\\\n• Security hardening & privacy minimal compliance done.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-design\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order DESIGN_PLAN_V1 from agent 2: **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – Design & Branding for Dunbar Oaks HOA**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nA. OBJECTIVE\\\\\\\\nCreate a simple, professional visual identity and apply it to a free, responsive WordPress site, then export a one-page style guide. All steps are deterministic and can be executed in sequence by any Administrator with WP back-end access (no code-level edits unless explicitly noted as *optional*).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nB. PRE-REQUISITES & DEPENDENCIES\\\\\\\\n1. WordPress ≥ 6.4 installed, user has Administrator role.\\\\\\\\n2. Required free plugins pre-installed but **not yet configured**:\\\\\\\\n   • Elementor (page builder)  \\\\\\\\n   • Elementor Header & Footer Builder OR Astra Widgets (optional)  \\\\\\\\n   • Customizer Export/Import  \\\\\\\\n   • SVG Support (for vector logo upload)\\\\\\\\n3. “Customizer > Additional CSS” panel remains enabled (default).\\\\\\\\n4. User can upload media ≤ 5 MB per file.\\\\\\\\n5. Infrastructure team whitelisted fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com (needed to load Google Fonts).\\\\\\\\n6. Assets to be collected from User before Step E-1 (see Section G).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nC. VISUAL IDENTITY SPECIFICATION\\\\\\\\n1. Color Palette (accessible contrast, WCAG AA):\\\\\\\\n   • PRIMARY – “Oak Green”   #356859  (rgb 53 ,104 , 89)   \\\\\\\\n   • SECONDARY – “Stone Sand” #E3B23C (rgb 227,178, 60)   \\\\\\\\n   • ACCENT – “Deep Teal”    #37967F (rgb 55 ,150 ,127)   \\\\\\\\n   • LIGHT NEUTRAL – “Linen” #F6F5F3 (rgb 246,245,243)   \\\\\\\\n   • DARK NEUTRAL – “Charcoal” #2F2F2F (rgb 47 , 47 , 47)\\\\\\\\n2. Typography (Google Fonts, free-to-use):\\\\\\\\n   • Headings (H1–H4) – \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Poppins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", weight 600  \\\\\\\\n   • Body / UI – \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Open Sans\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", weight 400/600  \\\\\\\\n   • Backup stack: “Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif”.\\\\\\\\n3. Logo Concept (to be produced/manually designed outside DEP):\\\\\\\\n   A minimal, flat oak-tree silhouette encircled by a thin ring; to the right, stacked text “Dunbar Oaks” (bold) above smaller “HOA” (regular). Single-color Oak Green on transparent background.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nD. THEME SELECTION & SET-UP\\\\\\\\nSTEP D-1  Install & Activate Theme\\\\\\\\n   • Navigate Appearance > Themes > Add New.  \\\\\\\\n   • Search “Astra”.  \\\\\\\\n   • Click Install → Activate.\\\\\\\\nSTEP D-2  Generate Child Theme (zero-code)\\\\\\\\n   • Visit https://wpastra.com/child-theme-generator/.  \\\\\\\\n   • Enter site name; download ZIP; upload via Appearance > Themes > Add New > Upload; Activate child theme.  \\\\\\\\n   (Keeps future CSS overrides isolated; no further edits required.)\\\\\\\\nSTEP D-3  Confirm responsive breakpoints (Astra default: 921 px tablet, 544 px mobile) – suits requirement; no change needed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nE. APPLY BRANDING (no-code unless flagged *)\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-1  Upload Logo/Favicon\\\\\\\\n   • Go to Appearance > Customize > Site Identity.  \\\\\\\\n   • Upload *logo.svg* (preferred) **512 × 512 px** or *logo.png* on transparent background.  \\\\\\\\n   • Set “Site Title” = blank (logo includes text).  \\\\\\\\n   • Upload *Site Icon* 512 × 512 px PNG.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-2  Set Global Colors\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Global > Colors.  \\\\\\\\n   • Base Color → PRIMARY (#356859).  \\\\\\\\n   • Link / Accent Color → ACCENT (#37967F).  \\\\\\\\n   • Heading Text → PRIMARY.  \\\\\\\\n   • Body Text → DARK NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Background → LIGHT NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-3  Configure Global Typography\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Global > Typography.  \\\\\\\\n   • Font Family –\\\\\\\\n       Headings: Poppins, 600.  \\\\\\\\n       Base: Open Sans, 400.  \\\\\\\\n   • Font Sizes (desktop): H1 = 42 px, H2 = 32 px, Base = 18 px.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.  \\\\\\\\n   *Optional code‐free*: If Astra’s built-in Google Fonts list lacks weights, install “Astra Custom Fonts” plugin.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-4  Build Header\\\\\\\\n   • Appearance > Astra Header Builder.  \\\\\\\\n   • Drag “Site Logo” left, “Primary Menu” center, “Button” (label “Pay Dues”) right with link to payment portal.  \\\\\\\\n   • Mobile – enable Off-Canvas Menu.  \\\\\\\\n   • Background Color → LIGHT NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Border bottom 2 px PRIMARY.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-5  Build Footer\\\\\\\\n   • Footer Builder → four-column layout.\\\\\\\\n       Col 1: Logo (50 px height).  \\\\\\\\n       Col 2: Quick Links menu.  \\\\\\\\n       Col 3: Address & contact (text).  \\\\\\\\n       Col 4: Social icons.  \\\\\\\\n   • Background color PRIMARY, text LIGHT NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-6  Navigation Styling\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Header > Primary Menu.  \\\\\\\\n   • Font: Poppins 600, size 16 px.  \\\\\\\\n   • Link hover color ACCENT.  \\\\\\\\n   • Active item underline 3 px ACCENT.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-7  Page Layout Defaults\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Global > Container.  \\\\\\\\n   • Width 1200 px; Inside Padding 2 rem.  \\\\\\\\n   • Blog Archive Layout: Grid 2 columns.  \\\\\\\\n   • Disable sidebar globally (can enable per-page later).\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-8  Import/Export Customizer Settings\\\\\\\\n   • Tools > Import/Export Customizer.  \\\\\\\\n   • Click “Export” → downloads .dat file (store for disaster recovery).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nF. ONE-PAGE STYLE-GUIDE EXPORT\\\\\\\\nSTEP F-1  Create Private Page\\\\\\\\n   • Pages > Add New → Title “Brand Style Guide”.  \\\\\\\\n   • Visibility: Private.  \\\\\\\\n   • Edit with Elementor.\\\\\\\\nSTEP F-2  Build Sections\\\\\\\\n   1. Hero heading “Dunbar Oaks HOA – Brand Guide” (H1).  \\\\\\\\n   2. Color Swatches: five columns (use “Inner Section”). For each color: 100 × 100 px box → background respective hex; below, text label & hex code.  \\\\\\\\n   3. Typography: two columns – left headings (H1–H4) sample text; right body paragraph sample.  \\\\\\\\n   4. Logo Usage: insert full-color logo (200 px), plus “Do/Don’t” list.  \\\\\\\\n   5. Iconography / Buttons: show primary button (Oak Green bg, light text) & link styling.\\\\\\\\nSTEP F-3  Export as PDF/Image\\\\\\\\n   • Elementor → icon ▸ Print to PDF ▸ “Save as PDF” A4 portrait.  \\\\\\\\n   • Rename file “DunbarOaks_StyleGuide_v1.pdf”; store in Media Library & download copy.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nG. ASSET REQUIREMENTS FROM USER\\\\\\\\n1. Final logo in SVG and 1024 × 1024 png.\\\\\\\\n2. Neighborhood hero image: **JPG, 1920 × 800 px**, ≤ 400 KB.\\\\\\\\n3. Committee/event photos: min 1200 × 800 px, landscape.\\\\\\\\n4. Payment-portal URL for header button.\\\\\\\\n5. Official address, phone, email, social URLs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nH. TECHNICAL HOOKS FOR INFRA/CMS TEAMS\\\\\\\\n1. Allow SVG uploads (plugin already installed); ensure `DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT` remains false until DEP executed.\\\\\\\\n2. Confirm caching layer excludes `/wp-json/` endpoints Elementer calls.\\\\\\\\n3. Schedule daily off-site backups (needed before customizer export import).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nI. VALIDATION CHECKLIST (post-execution)\\\\\\\\n☐ Logo displays crisp on desktop & mobile.  \\\\\\\\n☐ Colors match hex values across UI.  \\\\\\\\n☐ Google Fonts load in < 1 s (check DevTools).  \\\\\\\\n☐ Header/footer responsive.  \\\\\\\\n☐ Style Guide PDF stored & downloadable.  \\\\\\\\n☐ Customizer export file saved off-site.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:38:22.513Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify3###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"All three Directors have delivered detailed, fully-deterministic plans. To execute, we must confirm how the user wishes to handle sensitive access (AWS vs. registrar), and collect a few content/branding items the plans require. These answers unblock the Execution phase while keeping the process simple for a non-technical user.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1. To set up hosting we can (a) provision an AWS Lightsail WordPress server for about $5/month, or (b) use Namecheap’s EasyWP plan for roughly the same cost but with less future flexibility. Which option would you like us to proceed with?\\\",\\n    \\\"2. For whichever hosting option you choose, are you comfortable giving us temporary access (via a limited-privilege login or delegate link) to your domain registrar account for dunbaroakshoa.com so we can point the domain and add SSL, or would you prefer we give you step-by-step instructions to do that part yourself?\\\",\\n    \\\"3. What email address, phone number, and street address should appear on the site’s Contact page and receive inquiries from the contact form?\\\",\\n    \\\"4. Do you have a neighborhood photo (landscape, about 1920 × 800 px) you would like featured on the Home page hero section, or should we select a royalty-free placeholder image for you?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify3###\"}]},\"custom\":{}}],\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":14975,\"outputTokens\":1610,\"totalTokens\":16585},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-Bx0k2CD1ftsUosxvxvwn9X6WM7Dbi\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753403902,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###clarify3###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"All three Directors have delivered detailed, fully-deterministic plans. To execute, we must confirm how the user wishes to handle sensitive access (AWS vs. registrar), and collect a few content/branding items the plans require. These answers unblock the Execution phase while keeping the process simple for a non-technical user.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1. To set up hosting we can (a) provision an AWS Lightsail WordPress server for about $5/month, or (b) use Namecheap’s EasyWP plan for roughly the same cost but with less future flexibility. Which option would you like us to proceed with?\\\",\\n    \\\"2. For whichever hosting option you choose, are you comfortable giving us temporary access (via a limited-privilege login or delegate link) to your domain registrar account for dunbaroakshoa.com so we can point the domain and add SSL, or would you prefer we give you step-by-step instructions to do that part yourself?\\\",\\n    \\\"3. What email address, phone number, and street address should appear on the site’s Contact page and receive inquiries from the contact form?\\\",\\n    \\\"4. Do you have a neighborhood photo (landscape, about 1920 × 800 px) you would like featured on the Home page hero section, or should we select a royalty-free placeholder image for you?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify3###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":14975,\"completion_tokens\":1610,\"total_tokens\":16585,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":6784,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":1280,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"latencyMs\":43766.81733299978}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"openai/o3","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"600f22c238525756":{"spanId":"600f22c238525756","traceId":"70b7ee512dbfe2cadb5e130cdabda658","startTime":1753403902557,"endTime":1753403946329.2725,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"openai/o3\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure solution using any tech stack that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of the user's personal machine command line. Using the command line, you can create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, writing code, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and deploying applications.\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team (tokens) and in the context of the user (budget, cloud services, etc.). You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. **Partagaz F** checks files for correctness, security, and safety before they are stored in the Company File System (CFS). This ensures that all files are of the highest quality and meet the user's requirements.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Initial engagement: introduce myself as the user's Chief of Staff and discover their immediate need so we can begin planning and allocating resources appropriately.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Hello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. What can I create for you today?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:33:27.818Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. What can I create for you today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:33:27.818Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Gather essential details about hosting, user management, content, and preferences so we can propose an appropriate architecture, design, and implementation plan that matches the User’s technical comfort level and budget.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1. Do you already own a domain name for the HOA website, or would you like us to secure and configure one for you?\\\",\\n    \\\"2. Do you have a preferred hosting provider (e.g., GoDaddy, Squarespace, AWS) or would you like us to recommend an economical, secure option and manage it for you?\\\",\\n    \\\"3. Approximately how many residents will need login accounts, and do you prefer self-registration (e.g., residents sign up with a code) or administrator-created accounts?\\\",\\n    \\\"4. What kinds of files (PDF, Word, images, etc.) and approximate sizes will you upload for meeting minutes and financial reports?\\\",\\n    \\\"5. Will the Dues page simply list information, or would you like to accept online payments (credit card, ACH) through the site?\\\",\\n    \\\"6. Do you already have branding assets (logo, colors, photos) or would you like us to design/provide them?\\\",\\n    \\\"7. Would you like residents to receive email notifications/newsletters when new items are posted to News & Events?\\\",\\n    \\\"8. Do you have a target launch date or budget range in mind so we can tailor the solution accordingly?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify2###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:35:29.533Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1. Do you already own a domain name for the HOA website, or would you like us to secure and configure one for you?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2. Do you have a preferred hosting provider (e.g., GoDaddy, Squarespace, AWS) or would you like us to recommend an economical, secure option and manage it for you?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3. Approximately how many residents will need login accounts, and do you prefer self-registration (e.g., residents sign up with a code) or administrator-created accounts?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100, yes self-registration\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4. What kinds of files (PDF, Word, images, etc.) and approximate sizes will you upload for meeting minutes and financial reports?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"PDF files no more than 10 pages\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5. Will the Dues page simply list information, or would you like to accept online payments (credit card, ACH) through the site?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Simply list info\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"6. Do you already have branding assets (logo, colors, photos) or would you like us to design/provide them?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"7. Would you like residents to receive email notifications/newsletters when new items are posted to News & Events?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"8. Do you have a target launch date or budget range in mind so we can tailor the solution accordingly?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No, although as low as possible please\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:35:29.533Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###recruit-infra###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We need a high-level leader to plan low-cost, secure hosting, configure the existing domain (dunbaroakshoa.com), set up WordPress, SSL, backups, and lay out a deterministic infrastructure plan that other teams can rely on.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Infrastructure & Deployment\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"You are responsible for selecting economical hosting, configuring DNS/SSL, installing WordPress, and documenting an infrastructure DEP that other teams can follow.\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-infra###\\n###recruit-wp###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We require a senior specialist to architect the WordPress setup: create pages, select and configure plugins for authentication, self-registration, and protected content, ensuring usability for a non-technical HOA admin.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of CMS Implementation\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"You will design the WordPress information architecture, choose plugins (login, membership, contact form), define user roles, and produce a deterministic plan for implementing pages and protected sections.\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-wp###\\n###recruit-design###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"A dedicated design leader is needed to craft branding (logo, colors) and customize a responsive WordPress theme so the site looks polished yet remains easy to maintain.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Design & Branding\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Create a simple, professional visual identity, pick or modify a free theme, and document styling choices so non-technical admins can maintain consistency.\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-design###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:36:36.971Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-infra\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent F (4) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-wp\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Motti (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-design\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent D (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:36:36.971Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###order-infra###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Infrastructure & Deployment. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Select a low-cost, secure hosting approach suitable for ~100 WordPress users (e.g., reputable shared WP host or AWS Lightsail WP image) and compare at least two options with pricing, recommending one.\\\\n2. Detail exact setup steps: purchasing or linking the existing domain dunbaroakshoa.com, DNS changes, SSL (Let’s Encrypt or host-provided), automatic backups, and uptime monitoring—all with commands or provider UI clicks spelled out deterministically.\\\\n3. Include WordPress installation steps, staging ↔ production workflow, and basic hardening (firewall, limited login attempts, automatic updates).\\\\n4. Provide estimated recurring and one-time costs, and note any free-tier limits.\\\\n5. Specify any dependencies or information you need from the CMS & Design directors.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID INFRA_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"F\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"INFRA_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-infra###\\n###order-cms###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for CMS Implementation. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Define the WordPress information architecture: Home, Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings (protected), News & Events (protected).\\\\n2. Recommend and justify specific free/low-cost plugins for: a) resident self-registration (~100 users) with admin approval code; b) content protection/membership; c) simple page builder or block pattern for non-technical updates; d) contact form; e) PDF file management.\\\\n3. Outline exact configuration steps for each plugin, user-role definitions, and sample workflow for the HOA admin to upload/update protected content and news posts without coding.\\\\n4. Address basic security (CAPTCHA, limited login attempts) and privacy (no unnecessary data collection).\\\\n5. List any settings or theme hooks the Design director must accommodate and any hosting prerequisites from Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"Motti\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-cms###\\n###order-design###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Design & Branding. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Propose a simple, professional visual identity: color palette (3–5 colors), typography (Google Fonts), and a logo concept appropriate for Dunbar Oaks HOA.\\\\n2. Select a free, responsive WordPress theme that supports the CMS director’s plugin choices; outline any child-theme or Customizer tweaks needed.\\\\n3. Provide step-by-step instructions for applying the branding in WordPress (logo upload, colors, fonts) and for customizing key page layouts (header, footer, navigation) without coding where possible.\\\\n4. Export a one-page style guide (PDF or image) for future reference.\\\\n5. Note any asset sizes/formats required from the User (e.g., neighborhood photo) and any technical hooks that Infrastructure/CMS teams must enable.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID DESIGN_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"D\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DESIGN_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-design###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Malformed Call Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis automated message is to inform you that you that one or more of your attached system calls was not in the correct format.\\\\n\\\\nThe system program can only accept calls in the correct format. Please correct your call(s) and resubmit.\\\\n\\\\nSee below for the specific errors generated by your calls.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nCall ID order-infra failed inspection: Call order-infra of type ORDER failed inspection: recipient agent ID NaN does not exist.\\\"\\n}\\n###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###order-infra###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Infrastructure & Deployment. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Select a low-cost, secure hosting approach suitable for ~100 WordPress users (e.g., reputable shared WP host or AWS Lightsail WP image) and compare at least two options with pricing, recommending one.\\\\n2. Detail exact setup steps: purchasing or linking the existing domain dunbaroakshoa.com, DNS changes, SSL (Let’s Encrypt or host-provided), automatic backups, and uptime monitoring—spell out every command or provider UI action deterministically.\\\\n3. Include WordPress installation steps, staging ↔ production workflow, and basic hardening (firewall, limited login attempts, automatic updates).\\\\n4. Provide estimated recurring and one-time costs, and note any free-tier limits.\\\\n5. Specify any dependencies or information you need from the CMS & Design directors.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID INFRA_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"4\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"INFRA_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-infra###\\n###order-cms###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for CMS Implementation. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Define the WordPress information architecture: Home, Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings (protected), News & Events (protected).\\\\n2. Recommend and justify specific free/low-cost plugins for: a) resident self-registration (~100 users) with admin approval code; b) content protection/membership; c) simple page builder or block pattern for non-technical updates; d) contact form; e) PDF file management.\\\\n3. Outline exact configuration steps for each plugin, user-role definitions, and sample workflow for the HOA admin to upload/update protected content and news posts without coding.\\\\n4. Address basic security (CAPTCHA, limited login attempts) and privacy (no unnecessary data collection).\\\\n5. List any settings or theme hooks the Design director must accommodate and any hosting prerequisites from Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"3\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-cms###\\n###order-design###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Design & Branding. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Propose a simple, professional visual identity: color palette (3–5 colors), typography (Google Fonts), and a logo concept appropriate for Dunbar Oaks HOA.\\\\n2. Select a free, responsive WordPress theme that supports the CMS director’s plugin choices; outline any child-theme or Customizer tweaks needed.\\\\n3. Provide step-by-step instructions for applying the branding in WordPress (logo upload, colors, fonts) and for customizing key page layouts (header, footer, navigation) without coding where possible.\\\\n4. Export a one-page style guide (PDF or image) for future reference.\\\\n5. Note any asset sizes/formats required from the User (e.g., neighborhood photo) and any technical hooks that Infrastructure/CMS teams must enable.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID DESIGN_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"2\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DESIGN_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-design###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:38:22.513Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-infra\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order INFRA_PLAN_V1 from agent 4: INFRASTRUCTURE & DEPLOYMENT – DETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP)\\\\\\\\nSequence ID: INFRA_PLAN_V1\\\\\\\\nResponsible Agent: Director-rank (Hearts)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nA. OPTION COMPARISON & RECOMMENDATION\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nOption 1 – AWS Lightsail WordPress Blueprint\\\\\\\\n  • Instance (Plan) – 1 vCPU / 1 GB RAM / 40 GB SSD\\\\\\\\n  • Price – $5.00 USD / month flat (first month free)  \\\\\\\\n  • Data transfer – 2 TB included; overage $0.09/GB  \\\\\\\\n  • Snapshot backup – manual or scheduled, $0.05 / GB-month (≈$2 / mo for 40 GB)\\\\\\\\n  • Integrated DNS zones (free for first 3 zones), bundled static IP, built-in HTTPS via Let’s Encrypt, and one-click scaling.\\\\\\\\n  • Root SSH & WP admin access, security groups (firewall) configurable, AWS CLI available for IaC.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nOption 2 – Namecheap “EasyWP Turbo” Managed WordPress\\\\\\\\n  • Price – $4.88 USD / mo (annual billing) or $8.88 / mo monthly  \\\\\\\\n  • Visitors – up to 200 k/month, 1.5 CPU & 768 MB RAM burstable  \\\\\\\\n  • Storage – 25 GB SSD  \\\\\\\\n  • Free CDN and SSL (Sectigo)  \\\\\\\\n  • Backups – daily automatic (free), on-demand $2.00 each  \\\\\\\\n  • Limited root / plugin control; no AWS-grade scalability.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRecommendation: AWS Lightsail WordPress Blueprint.\\\\\\\\n  – Similar pricing; stronger scalability path (upgrade instance or migrate to EC2/EKS), granular firewall rules, snapshot-level backups, CLI automation, and easier multi-environment cloning.  \\\\\\\\n  – Includes 1 static IP & free monthly cost credits for first month.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nB. HIGH-LEVEL DEPENDENCIES\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nD1. Registrar credentials for dunbaroakshoa.com (assumed currently at GoDaddy).  \\\\\\\\nD2. AWS root or IAM user with Lightsail + Route 53 + Certificate Manager permissions.  \\\\\\\\nD3. CMS/Design team to supply: (a) chosen WP theme & plugins list, (b) branding assets, (c) staging content requirements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nC. STEP-BY-STEP EXECUTION – FULLY DETERMINISTIC\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nNOTE: Steps are numbered; execute sequentially. Commands prefixed “$” are run from an authorized local shell with AWS CLI v2 configured (profile «do-hoa»). UI clicks use exact menu paths.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 0. Local Workstation Prep ——\\\\\\\\n0.1  Install AWS CLI v2 & Lightsailctl plugin (if not present):\\\\\\\\n     $ curl \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -o awscliv2.zip\\\\\\\\n     $ unzip awscliv2.zip && sudo ./aws/install\\\\\\\\n     $ pip install awscli-plugin-lightsail\\\\\\\\n0.2  Configure profile with least-privilege IAM creds:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws configure --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n     (enter Access Key, Secret, us-east-1, json)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 1. Networking & DNS ——\\\\\\\\n1.1  Create Route 53 public hosted zone (if DNS will migrate):\\\\\\\\n     $ aws route53 create-hosted-zone --name dunbaroakshoa.com --caller-reference $(date +%s) --profile do-hoa > /tmp/zone.json\\\\\\\\n     Record HostedZoneId = $(jq -r '.HostedZone.Id' /tmp/zone.json)\\\\\\\\n1.2  If keeping registrar DNS, skip 1.1 and obtain existing control panel.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 2. Lightsail Instance Provisioning ——\\\\\\\\n2.1  Allocate static IP:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail allocate-static-ip --static-ip-name do-prod-ip --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n2.2  Create production instance:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail create-instances \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --instance-names do-prod-wp \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --availability-zone us-east-1a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --blueprint-id wordpress \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --bundle-id micro_2_0 (represents 1GB/40GB) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --user-data file://disable_ping.sh \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n2.3  Attach static IP:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail attach-static-ip --static-ip-name do-prod-ip --instance-name do-prod-wp --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n2.4  Repeat 2.1-2.3 with names do-stage-ip / do-stage-wp for staging environment.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 3. DNS Records ——\\\\\\\\n3.1  Create A record \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"@\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" → static prod IP & CNAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"www\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" → dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\n     If Route 53:\\\\\\\\n     $ cat > /tmp/rr.json <<EOF\\\\\\\\n     {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Comment\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A + CNAME\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Changes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"UPSERT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecordSet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TTL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":300,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecords\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"<PROD_IP>\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"UPSERT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecordSet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"www.dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CNAME\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TTL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":300,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecords\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}}]}\\\\\\\\n     EOF\\\\\\\\n     $ aws route53 change-resource-record-sets --hosted-zone-id $HostedZoneId --change-batch file:///tmp/rr.json --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n3.2  At registrar, replace nameservers with those from Route 53 OR create A/CNAME records if staying.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 4. SSL/TLS Certificates ——\\\\\\\\n4.1  In Lightsail console → Networking → HTTPS → “Enable HTTPS” → Let’s Encrypt → pick dunbaroakshoa.com + www. System auto-installs certbot & cron renewals. Deterministic via CLI:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail create-certificate --certificate-name do-cert --domain-name dunbaroakshoa.com --subject-alternative-names www.dunbaroakshoa.com --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail attach-certificate-to-distribution ... (Lightsail auto-distribution optional)\\\\\\\\n4.2  Verify `https://dunbaroakshoa.com` green padlock in browser.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 5. WordPress Initialisation ——\\\\\\\\n5.1  Retrieve WP admin password:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail get-instance --instance-name do-prod-wp --profile do-hoa | jq -r '.instance.username'\\\\\\\\n     ssh bitnami@<PROD_IP>\\\\\\\\n     $ cat ~/bitnami_application_password\\\\\\\\n5.2  Log into `https://dunbaroakshoa.com/wp-admin`, change password, set site title.\\\\\\\\n5.3  Install plugin “Limit Login Attempts Reloaded” (Security → Add New → search).\\\\\\\\n5.4  Enable automatic WP core/theme/plugin updates: Dashboard → Updates → “Enable automatic”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 6. Staging ↔ Production Workflow ——\\\\\\\\n6.1  Stage site lives on do-stage-wp, IP e.g., 3.3.3.3, DNS: staging.dunbaroakshoa.com (A record).\\\\\\\\n6.2  Deploy Pipeline (manual deterministic):\\\\\\\\n     a) WP Plugin “All-in-One WP Migration” installed on both envs.  \\\\\\\\n     b) On staging: Export → File.  \\\\\\\\n     c) scp file to local or directly import on production.  \\\\\\\\n     (Future: Implement Lightsail Snapshots & AWS CodePipeline for blue-green; out of scope but feasible.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 7. Backups ——\\\\\\\\n7.1  Automated snapshot schedule (daily, retain 7):\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail put-instance-public-ports --instance-name do-prod-wp --port-infos file://ports.json --profile do-hoa  # (allows snapshot API)\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail create-auto-snapshot-add-on --instance-name do-prod-wp --add-on-type AutoSnapshot --status Enabled --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n7.2  Confirm: $ aws lightsail get-auto-snapshots --instance-name do-prod-wp --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n7.3  Repeat for staging.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 8. Uptime Monitoring ——\\\\\\\\n8.1  Enable Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics (free for 100 canaries-runs per month in Free Tier):\\\\\\\\n     $ aws synthetics create-canary --name do-home-canary --code S3Bucket=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"synthetics-bucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",S3Key=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ping.zip\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --execution-role-arn <ROLE> --schedule \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rate(5 minutes)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --run-config timeoutInSeconds=60 --artifact-s3-location s3://synthetics-artifacts/ --runtime-version syn-nodejs-puppeteer-3.4 --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n8.2  Alarm: 2 consecutive failures triggers SNS → email admin.\\\\\\\\n     (Alternatively, use free UptimeRobot monitor if AWS budget sensitive.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 9. Firewall Hardening ——\\\\\\\\n9.1  Default Lightsail firewall: Allow 80/tcp, 443/tcp, 22/tcp (SSH) from owner IP only; disable ping.\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail open-instance-public-ports --instance-name do-prod-wp --port-info fromPort=22,toPort=22,protocol=TCP,cidr=<OFFICE_IP>/32 --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n9.2  Disable XML-RPC: WP plugin “Disable XMLRPC-Pingback”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 10. Post-Deployment Validation ——\\\\\\\\n10.1  SSL Labs test score ≥ A.  \\\\\\\\n10.2  Wordfence scan passes; login attempts limited.  \\\\\\\\n10.3  CloudWatch canary status OK.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nD. COST SUMMARY (USD)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nRECURRING\\\\\\\\n  • Lightsail Prod instance: $5.00 / mo\\\\\\\\n  • Lightsail Stage instance: $5.00 / mo (can be stopped when idle to <$1)\\\\\\\\n  • Snapshots (~40 GB each): 2 × $2.00 ≈ $4.00 / mo\\\\\\\\n  • Route 53 Hosted Zone: $0.50 / mo + $0.40 / million queries (negligible)\\\\\\\\n  • CloudWatch Canaries: <$1 in Free Tier (first year) ⇒ then $4.50 / mo if 5-min interval\\\\\\\\nTotal steady-state ≈ $14.50 – $18.00 / month\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nONE-TIME\\\\\\\\n  • Domain transfer (if moving registrars): ~$9.00 (includes 1-year renewal)  \\\\\\\\n  • Initial snapshot storage grows linearly but negligible (<$1) first month\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFREE-TIER / NO-COST ITEMS\\\\\\\\n  • First Lightsail month free  \\\\\\\\n  • Let’s Encrypt SSL  \\\\\\\\n  • Up to 3 Route 53 DNS health checks free for 12 months  \\\\\\\\n  • AWS Free Tier 1 GB snapshot storage  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nE. HAND-OFF ARTIFACTS\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nE1. Generated HostedZoneId and static IPs – to be documented in shared secrets vault.\\\\\\\\nE2. Saved AWS CLI commands log (/var/log/infra-deploy-$(date).log) for audit.\\\\\\\\nE3. CloudFormation template (optional) to codify steps 2-7 – can be produced on request.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nF. NEXT-STE P REQUESTS TO CMS / DESIGN DIRECTORS\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nF1. Confirm choice of theme/plugins so we can pre-install in AMI snapshot.  \\\\\\\\nF2. Supply favicon & logo to complete staging site before production push.  \\\\\\\\nF3. Provide colour palette to configure CDN edge rules for image optimisation (optional).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nEnd of DEP – ready for Partagaz D review.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-cms\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order CMS_PLAN_V1 from agent 3: **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – CMS_PLAN_V1**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nA. HOSTING & BASELINE\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Hosting prerequisites (Infrastructure team)\\\\\\\\n   a. PHP ≥ 8.1, memory_limit ≥ 256 M, max_upload_filesize ≥ 32 M.\\\\\\\\n   b. MariaDB 10.5 / MySQL 8.0, InnoDB default.\\\\\\\\n   c. HTTPS enabled (Let’s Encrypt or other TLS cert) before public launch.\\\\\\\\n   d. Cron jobs allowed (for WP‐Cron replacement if traffic < 1k/day this can stay virtual).\\\\\\\\n   e. SMTP credentials or transactional-mail service (Postmark / SendGrid free tier) for registration emails.\\\\\\\\n   f. File-system write permissions for wp-content and install zip uploads.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Fresh WordPress 6.5.x install in root directory; enforce automatic minor/major core updates:\\\\\\\\n   wp-config.php →\\\\\\\\n   define('WP_AUTO_UPDATE_CORE','minor');\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Theme baseline picked by Design director: “Twenty Twenty-Four” **or** “Astra Free”.\\\\\\\\n   • Must support: full-site-editing (FSE) hooks `header`, `footer`, `sidebar` if Astra.\\\\\\\\n   • Keep child-theme blank (style.css, functions.php) reserved for any CSS/JS overrides but *initially empty* to keep DEP deterministic.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nB. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE (IA)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nCreate pages in this exact slug order:\\\\\\\\n1. `/`  → “Home”\\\\\\\\n2. `/contact-us/` → “Contact Us”\\\\\\\\n3. `/bylaws/` → “HOA Bylaws” (public)\\\\\\\\n4. `/schools/` → “Nearby Schools” (public)\\\\\\\\n5. `/dues/` → “Dues” (PROTECTED)\\\\\\\\n6. `/annual-meetings/` → “Annual Meetings” (PROTECTED)\\\\\\\\n7. `/news-events/` → “News & Events” (PROTECTED)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNavigation menu “Main Menu” created and assigned to Theme primary location using identical order.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nC. PLUGIN STACK (all free unless noted)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. User self-registration + manual admin approval + access-code field\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“User Registration – Custom Registration Form, Login and User Profile”** by WP Everest.\\\\\\\\n     – Free tier supports manual approval, custom fields & form shortcodes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Content/membership protection\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Content Control – User Access Restriction”** by Code Atlantic (100 % free, no paywall).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Simple page/block builder for non-technical updates\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Kadence Blocks – Gutenberg Blocks for Page Builder Features”** (free) – adds pre-made block patterns, accordions, tabs; stays inside core editor.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Contact form with CAPTCHA\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“WPForms Lite”** (free) – includes hCaptcha & reCAPTCHA v2/v3 support.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. PDF file management / embed & protection\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“EmbedPress”** (free) – Gutenberg block to embed PDF inline.\\\\\\\\n   • **“Prevent Direct Access – PDA Lite”** (free) – protects PDFs so file URLs respect membership rules.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Security hardening\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Limit Login Attempts Reloaded”** (free).\\\\\\\\n   • (Optional) “WP 2FA” free module if MFA desired later.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Role/Capability management convenience\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Members”** by MemberPress (free) – create Custom Role “Resident”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nD. STEP-BY-STEP CONFIGURATION\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nD1. Global order of operations (deterministic):\\\\\\\\n   1. Complete WP install (A2).\\\\\\\\n   2. Install theme (A3).\\\\\\\\n   3. Install *all* plugins in section C but keep them **deactivated**.\\\\\\\\n   4. Activate plugins sequentially in this exact order to avoid capability conflicts:\\\\\\\\n      a. Members\\\\\\\\n      b. User Registration\\\\\\\\n      c. Content Control\\\\\\\\n      d. Kadence Blocks\\\\\\\\n      e. WPForms Lite\\\\\\\\n      f. EmbedPress\\\\\\\\n      g. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite\\\\\\\\n      h. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\\\\\n   5. Create roles, forms, rules as below.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD2. Members plugin – role definitions\\\\\\\\n   • Create custom role **Resident**.\\\\\\\\n     Capabilities: `read`, `edit_posts` = false, `upload_files` = false. (Leave all others unchecked.)\\\\\\\\n   • (Core) Keep Administrator, Editor defaults.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD3. User Registration plugin – registration form\\\\\\\\n   1. Create new form “Resident Signup”.\\\\\\\\n   2. Add core fields: First Name, Last Name, Email (username), Password.\\\\\\\\n   3. Add custom Text field “Access Code”.\\\\\\\\n      – Field meta-key: `hoa_access_code`.\\\\\\\\n      – Field set as *required*.\\\\\\\\n   4. Enable *Manual Admin Approval* (Settings ▸ General ▸ User Login Option ▸ “Admin Approve”).\\\\\\\\n   5. Form setting ▸ *Enable email confirmation* = OFF (because approval already required).\\\\\\\\n   6. Place validation rule via form *Field Visibility & Logic*:\\\\\\\\n      – If `hoa_access_code` ≠ “NEIGHBOR2024” (example), display error “Invalid HOA code”.\\\\\\\\n   7. Save form; copy generated shortcode `[user_registration_form id=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"XX\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]`.\\\\\\\\n   8. Create WordPress page `/register/` titled “Resident Registration”, paste shortcode.\\\\\\\\n   9. In WP ▸ Settings ▸ General ▸ “Membership – Anyone can register” = **unchecked** (security).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD4. Content Control – protection rules\\\\\\\\n   • Rule 1: Protect Pages `Dues`, `Annual Meetings`, `News & Events`.\\\\\\\\n     – Access condition: Logged-in users with role = Resident OR ≥ Editor.\\\\\\\\n     – Redirect on failure: `/register/` (or custom message page).\\\\\\\\n   • Rule 2: Protect Media Files category “Protected PDFs” (auto-created by PDA Lite) with same role condition.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD5. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite – PDF handling\\\\\\\\n   1. Settings ▸ Permalink Type: “Encrypted URL” (default).\\\\\\\\n   2. Upload PDF → Media Library → toggle “Protect this file”.\\\\\\\\n   3. Copy shortcode `[pda_protected url=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" download=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]` and insert inside protected pages.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD6. WPForms Lite – contact form\\\\\\\\n   1. Create form “HOA Contact”. Fields: Name, Email, Message.\\\\\\\\n   2. Settings ▸ Spam Protection → enable Google reCAPTCHA v3 (site key provided separately by Infrastructure).\\\\\\\\n   3. Notifications → send to `hoaboard@example.com`.\\\\\\\\n   4. Embed form in “Contact Us” page using Gutenberg block.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD7. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\\\\\n   • Settings → Lockout at 4 retries, 30 min lockout, 24 h increase, GDPR consent banner OFF.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD8. Kadence Blocks (non-technical editing enablement)\\\\\\\\n   • Install Starter Templates if Astra theme chosen; else use built-in patterns.\\\\\\\\n   • Provide training doc (outside DEP) listing: Accordion (meeting minutes), Info Box (dues summary), Gallery (events photos).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nE. SAMPLE WORKFLOWS\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Resident onboarding\\\\\\\\n   a. User visits /register/; enters data + HOA access code.\\\\\\\\n   b. Admin receives email “User Registration Requires Approval”.\\\\\\\\n   c. Admin logs in → User Registration ▸ Users → Approve.\\\\\\\\n   d. User receives “Your account is approved” email, logs in, sees protected menu items.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. HOA Admin uploads protected PDF (e.g., Annual Meeting Minutes)\\\\\\\\n   a. Media ▸ Add New → upload PDF → click “Protect this file”.\\\\\\\\n   b. Copy auto-generated shortcode.\\\\\\\\n   c. Edit “Annual Meetings” page (block editor) → add ‘Shortcode’ block → paste.\\\\\\\\n   d. Click Update; file now downloadable only by Residents.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Post News item\\\\\\\\n   a. Posts ▸ Add New → title + content; set Category = “Members Only News”.\\\\\\\\n   b. Content Control rule can also blanket-protect this category if preferred (create Rule 3 referencing category).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nF. SECURITY / PRIVACY CHECKLIST\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n✔ SSL mandatory.\\\\\\\\n✔ Limit Login Attempts active.\\\\\\\\n✔ reCAPTCHA on Contact form.\\\\\\\\n✔ Manual approval prevents spam users.\\\\\\\\n✔ Only essential PII collected (name, email, HOA access code). No DOB, phone, etc.\\\\\\\\n✔ Weekly automated backups via host or UpdraftPlus (free) – schedule to external storage (Google Drive free tier).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nG. DESIGN TEAM HOOKS & NOTES\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Theme must output `wp_nav_menu()` location “primary”.\\\\\\\\n2. Register sidebar “Protected Sidebar” (optional) if theme offers sidebars → may hold quick-links visible only to Residents via `is_user_logged_in()`.\\\\\\\\n3. Ensure CSS for `.pda-protected` shortcode wrapper inherits theme typography.\\\\\\\\n4. If using Astra, keep header builder; add custom menu item CSS class `menu-item-protected` (style to match but hide via `display:none` unauth if plugin flashes). Not needed for FSE theme.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nH. DELIVERABLE SUMMARY\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• Working WordPress site with defined IA, plugins configured, roles created.\\\\\\\\n• No paid licenses required; all plugins on WP.org repo.\\\\\\\\n• Non-technical HOA admins can manage protected documents and news via Gutenberg + Kadence Blocks.\\\\\\\\n• Security hardening & privacy minimal compliance done.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-design\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order DESIGN_PLAN_V1 from agent 2: **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – Design & Branding for Dunbar Oaks HOA**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nA. OBJECTIVE\\\\\\\\nCreate a simple, professional visual identity and apply it to a free, responsive WordPress site, then export a one-page style guide. All steps are deterministic and can be executed in sequence by any Administrator with WP back-end access (no code-level edits unless explicitly noted as *optional*).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nB. PRE-REQUISITES & DEPENDENCIES\\\\\\\\n1. WordPress ≥ 6.4 installed, user has Administrator role.\\\\\\\\n2. Required free plugins pre-installed but **not yet configured**:\\\\\\\\n   • Elementor (page builder)  \\\\\\\\n   • Elementor Header & Footer Builder OR Astra Widgets (optional)  \\\\\\\\n   • Customizer Export/Import  \\\\\\\\n   • SVG Support (for vector logo upload)\\\\\\\\n3. “Customizer > Additional CSS” panel remains enabled (default).\\\\\\\\n4. User can upload media ≤ 5 MB per file.\\\\\\\\n5. Infrastructure team whitelisted fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com (needed to load Google Fonts).\\\\\\\\n6. Assets to be collected from User before Step E-1 (see Section G).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nC. VISUAL IDENTITY SPECIFICATION\\\\\\\\n1. Color Palette (accessible contrast, WCAG AA):\\\\\\\\n   • PRIMARY – “Oak Green”   #356859  (rgb 53 ,104 , 89)   \\\\\\\\n   • SECONDARY – “Stone Sand” #E3B23C (rgb 227,178, 60)   \\\\\\\\n   • ACCENT – “Deep Teal”    #37967F (rgb 55 ,150 ,127)   \\\\\\\\n   • LIGHT NEUTRAL – “Linen” #F6F5F3 (rgb 246,245,243)   \\\\\\\\n   • DARK NEUTRAL – “Charcoal” #2F2F2F (rgb 47 , 47 , 47)\\\\\\\\n2. Typography (Google Fonts, free-to-use):\\\\\\\\n   • Headings (H1–H4) – \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Poppins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", weight 600  \\\\\\\\n   • Body / UI – \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Open Sans\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", weight 400/600  \\\\\\\\n   • Backup stack: “Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif”.\\\\\\\\n3. Logo Concept (to be produced/manually designed outside DEP):\\\\\\\\n   A minimal, flat oak-tree silhouette encircled by a thin ring; to the right, stacked text “Dunbar Oaks” (bold) above smaller “HOA” (regular). Single-color Oak Green on transparent background.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nD. THEME SELECTION & SET-UP\\\\\\\\nSTEP D-1  Install & Activate Theme\\\\\\\\n   • Navigate Appearance > Themes > Add New.  \\\\\\\\n   • Search “Astra”.  \\\\\\\\n   • Click Install → Activate.\\\\\\\\nSTEP D-2  Generate Child Theme (zero-code)\\\\\\\\n   • Visit https://wpastra.com/child-theme-generator/.  \\\\\\\\n   • Enter site name; download ZIP; upload via Appearance > Themes > Add New > Upload; Activate child theme.  \\\\\\\\n   (Keeps future CSS overrides isolated; no further edits required.)\\\\\\\\nSTEP D-3  Confirm responsive breakpoints (Astra default: 921 px tablet, 544 px mobile) – suits requirement; no change needed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nE. APPLY BRANDING (no-code unless flagged *)\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-1  Upload Logo/Favicon\\\\\\\\n   • Go to Appearance > Customize > Site Identity.  \\\\\\\\n   • Upload *logo.svg* (preferred) **512 × 512 px** or *logo.png* on transparent background.  \\\\\\\\n   • Set “Site Title” = blank (logo includes text).  \\\\\\\\n   • Upload *Site Icon* 512 × 512 px PNG.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-2  Set Global Colors\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Global > Colors.  \\\\\\\\n   • Base Color → PRIMARY (#356859).  \\\\\\\\n   • Link / Accent Color → ACCENT (#37967F).  \\\\\\\\n   • Heading Text → PRIMARY.  \\\\\\\\n   • Body Text → DARK NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Background → LIGHT NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-3  Configure Global Typography\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Global > Typography.  \\\\\\\\n   • Font Family –\\\\\\\\n       Headings: Poppins, 600.  \\\\\\\\n       Base: Open Sans, 400.  \\\\\\\\n   • Font Sizes (desktop): H1 = 42 px, H2 = 32 px, Base = 18 px.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.  \\\\\\\\n   *Optional code‐free*: If Astra’s built-in Google Fonts list lacks weights, install “Astra Custom Fonts” plugin.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-4  Build Header\\\\\\\\n   • Appearance > Astra Header Builder.  \\\\\\\\n   • Drag “Site Logo” left, “Primary Menu” center, “Button” (label “Pay Dues”) right with link to payment portal.  \\\\\\\\n   • Mobile – enable Off-Canvas Menu.  \\\\\\\\n   • Background Color → LIGHT NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Border bottom 2 px PRIMARY.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-5  Build Footer\\\\\\\\n   • Footer Builder → four-column layout.\\\\\\\\n       Col 1: Logo (50 px height).  \\\\\\\\n       Col 2: Quick Links menu.  \\\\\\\\n       Col 3: Address & contact (text).  \\\\\\\\n       Col 4: Social icons.  \\\\\\\\n   • Background color PRIMARY, text LIGHT NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-6  Navigation Styling\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Header > Primary Menu.  \\\\\\\\n   • Font: Poppins 600, size 16 px.  \\\\\\\\n   • Link hover color ACCENT.  \\\\\\\\n   • Active item underline 3 px ACCENT.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-7  Page Layout Defaults\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Global > Container.  \\\\\\\\n   • Width 1200 px; Inside Padding 2 rem.  \\\\\\\\n   • Blog Archive Layout: Grid 2 columns.  \\\\\\\\n   • Disable sidebar globally (can enable per-page later).\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-8  Import/Export Customizer Settings\\\\\\\\n   • Tools > Import/Export Customizer.  \\\\\\\\n   • Click “Export” → downloads .dat file (store for disaster recovery).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nF. ONE-PAGE STYLE-GUIDE EXPORT\\\\\\\\nSTEP F-1  Create Private Page\\\\\\\\n   • Pages > Add New → Title “Brand Style Guide”.  \\\\\\\\n   • Visibility: Private.  \\\\\\\\n   • Edit with Elementor.\\\\\\\\nSTEP F-2  Build Sections\\\\\\\\n   1. Hero heading “Dunbar Oaks HOA – Brand Guide” (H1).  \\\\\\\\n   2. Color Swatches: five columns (use “Inner Section”). For each color: 100 × 100 px box → background respective hex; below, text label & hex code.  \\\\\\\\n   3. Typography: two columns – left headings (H1–H4) sample text; right body paragraph sample.  \\\\\\\\n   4. Logo Usage: insert full-color logo (200 px), plus “Do/Don’t” list.  \\\\\\\\n   5. Iconography / Buttons: show primary button (Oak Green bg, light text) & link styling.\\\\\\\\nSTEP F-3  Export as PDF/Image\\\\\\\\n   • Elementor → icon ▸ Print to PDF ▸ “Save as PDF” A4 portrait.  \\\\\\\\n   • Rename file “DunbarOaks_StyleGuide_v1.pdf”; store in Media Library & download copy.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nG. ASSET REQUIREMENTS FROM USER\\\\\\\\n1. Final logo in SVG and 1024 × 1024 png.\\\\\\\\n2. Neighborhood hero image: **JPG, 1920 × 800 px**, ≤ 400 KB.\\\\\\\\n3. Committee/event photos: min 1200 × 800 px, landscape.\\\\\\\\n4. Payment-portal URL for header button.\\\\\\\\n5. Official address, phone, email, social URLs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nH. TECHNICAL HOOKS FOR INFRA/CMS TEAMS\\\\\\\\n1. Allow SVG uploads (plugin already installed); ensure `DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT` remains false until DEP executed.\\\\\\\\n2. Confirm caching layer excludes `/wp-json/` endpoints Elementer calls.\\\\\\\\n3. Schedule daily off-site backups (needed before customizer export import).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nI. VALIDATION CHECKLIST (post-execution)\\\\\\\\n☐ Logo displays crisp on desktop & mobile.  \\\\\\\\n☐ Colors match hex values across UI.  \\\\\\\\n☐ Google Fonts load in < 1 s (check DevTools).  \\\\\\\\n☐ Header/footer responsive.  \\\\\\\\n☐ Style Guide PDF stored & downloadable.  \\\\\\\\n☐ Customizer export file saved off-site.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:38:22.513Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify3###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"All three Directors have delivered detailed, fully-deterministic plans. To execute, we must confirm how the user wishes to handle sensitive access (AWS vs. registrar), and collect a few content/branding items the plans require. These answers unblock the Execution phase while keeping the process simple for a non-technical user.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1. To set up hosting we can (a) provision an AWS Lightsail WordPress server for about $5/month, or (b) use Namecheap’s EasyWP plan for roughly the same cost but with less future flexibility. Which option would you like us to proceed with?\\\",\\n    \\\"2. For whichever hosting option you choose, are you comfortable giving us temporary access (via a limited-privilege login or delegate link) to your domain registrar account for dunbaroakshoa.com so we can point the domain and add SSL, or would you prefer we give you step-by-step instructions to do that part yourself?\\\",\\n    \\\"3. What email address, phone number, and street address should appear on the site’s Contact page and receive inquiries from the contact form?\\\",\\n    \\\"4. Do you have a neighborhood photo (landscape, about 1920 × 800 px) you would like featured on the Home page hero section, or should we select a royalty-free placeholder image for you?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify3###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":14975,\"outputTokens\":1610,\"totalTokens\":16585},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-Bx0k2CD1ftsUosxvxvwn9X6WM7Dbi\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753403902,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###clarify3###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"All three Directors have delivered detailed, fully-deterministic plans. To execute, we must confirm how the user wishes to handle sensitive access (AWS vs. registrar), and collect a few content/branding items the plans require. These answers unblock the Execution phase while keeping the process simple for a non-technical user.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1. To set up hosting we can (a) provision an AWS Lightsail WordPress server for about $5/month, or (b) use Namecheap’s EasyWP plan for roughly the same cost but with less future flexibility. Which option would you like us to proceed with?\\\",\\n    \\\"2. For whichever hosting option you choose, are you comfortable giving us temporary access (via a limited-privilege login or delegate link) to your domain registrar account for dunbaroakshoa.com so we can point the domain and add SSL, or would you prefer we give you step-by-step instructions to do that part yourself?\\\",\\n    \\\"3. What email address, phone number, and street address should appear on the site’s Contact page and receive inquiries from the contact form?\\\",\\n    \\\"4. Do you have a neighborhood photo (landscape, about 1920 × 800 px) you would like featured on the Home page hero section, or should we select a royalty-free placeholder image for you?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify3###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":14975,\"completion_tokens\":1610,\"total_tokens\":16585,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":6784,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":1280,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"request\":{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure solution using any tech stack that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of the user's personal machine command line. Using the command line, you can create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, writing code, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and deploying applications.\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team (tokens) and in the context of the user (budget, cloud services, etc.). You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. **Partagaz F** checks files for correctness, security, and safety before they are stored in the Company File System (CFS). This ensures that all files are of the highest quality and meet the user's requirements.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Initial engagement: introduce myself as the user's Chief of Staff and discover their immediate need so we can begin planning and allocating resources appropriately.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Hello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. What can I create for you today?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:33:27.818Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. What can I create for you today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:33:27.818Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Gather essential details about hosting, user management, content, and preferences so we can propose an appropriate architecture, design, and implementation plan that matches the User’s technical comfort level and budget.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1. Do you already own a domain name for the HOA website, or would you like us to secure and configure one for you?\\\",\\n    \\\"2. Do you have a preferred hosting provider (e.g., GoDaddy, Squarespace, AWS) or would you like us to recommend an economical, secure option and manage it for you?\\\",\\n    \\\"3. Approximately how many residents will need login accounts, and do you prefer self-registration (e.g., residents sign up with a code) or administrator-created accounts?\\\",\\n    \\\"4. What kinds of files (PDF, Word, images, etc.) and approximate sizes will you upload for meeting minutes and financial reports?\\\",\\n    \\\"5. Will the Dues page simply list information, or would you like to accept online payments (credit card, ACH) through the site?\\\",\\n    \\\"6. Do you already have branding assets (logo, colors, photos) or would you like us to design/provide them?\\\",\\n    \\\"7. Would you like residents to receive email notifications/newsletters when new items are posted to News & Events?\\\",\\n    \\\"8. Do you have a target launch date or budget range in mind so we can tailor the solution accordingly?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify2###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:35:29.533Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1. Do you already own a domain name for the HOA website, or would you like us to secure and configure one for you?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2. Do you have a preferred hosting provider (e.g., GoDaddy, Squarespace, AWS) or would you like us to recommend an economical, secure option and manage it for you?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3. Approximately how many residents will need login accounts, and do you prefer self-registration (e.g., residents sign up with a code) or administrator-created accounts?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100, yes self-registration\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4. What kinds of files (PDF, Word, images, etc.) and approximate sizes will you upload for meeting minutes and financial reports?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"PDF files no more than 10 pages\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5. Will the Dues page simply list information, or would you like to accept online payments (credit card, ACH) through the site?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Simply list info\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"6. Do you already have branding assets (logo, colors, photos) or would you like us to design/provide them?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"7. Would you like residents to receive email notifications/newsletters when new items are posted to News & Events?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"8. Do you have a target launch date or budget range in mind so we can tailor the solution accordingly?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No, although as low as possible please\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:35:29.533Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###recruit-infra###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We need a high-level leader to plan low-cost, secure hosting, configure the existing domain (dunbaroakshoa.com), set up WordPress, SSL, backups, and lay out a deterministic infrastructure plan that other teams can rely on.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Infrastructure & Deployment\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"You are responsible for selecting economical hosting, configuring DNS/SSL, installing WordPress, and documenting an infrastructure DEP that other teams can follow.\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-infra###\\n###recruit-wp###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We require a senior specialist to architect the WordPress setup: create pages, select and configure plugins for authentication, self-registration, and protected content, ensuring usability for a non-technical HOA admin.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of CMS Implementation\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"You will design the WordPress information architecture, choose plugins (login, membership, contact form), define user roles, and produce a deterministic plan for implementing pages and protected sections.\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-wp###\\n###recruit-design###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"A dedicated design leader is needed to craft branding (logo, colors) and customize a responsive WordPress theme so the site looks polished yet remains easy to maintain.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Design & Branding\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"Create a simple, professional visual identity, pick or modify a free theme, and document styling choices so non-technical admins can maintain consistency.\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-design###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:36:36.971Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\