,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"INFRA_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-infra###\\n###order-cms###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for CMS Implementation. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Define the WordPress information architecture: Home, Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings (protected), News & Events (protected).\\\\n2. Recommend and justify specific free/low-cost plugins for: a) resident self-registration (~100 users) with admin approval code; b) content protection/membership; c) simple page builder or block pattern for non-technical updates; d) contact form; e) PDF file management.\\\\n3. Outline exact configuration steps for each plugin, user-role definitions, and sample workflow for the HOA admin to upload/update protected content and news posts without coding.\\\\n4. Address basic security (CAPTCHA, limited login attempts) and privacy (no unnecessary data collection).\\\\n5. List any settings or theme hooks the Design director must accommodate and any hosting prerequisites from Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"Motti\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-cms###\\n###order-design###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Design & Branding. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Propose a simple, professional visual identity: color palette (3–5 colors), typography (Google Fonts), and a logo concept appropriate for Dunbar Oaks HOA.\\\\n2. Select a free, responsive WordPress theme that supports the CMS director’s plugin choices; outline any child-theme or Customizer tweaks needed.\\\\n3. Provide step-by-step instructions for applying the branding in WordPress (logo upload, colors, fonts) and for customizing key page layouts (header, footer, navigation) without coding where possible.\\\\n4. Export a one-page style guide (PDF or image) for future reference.\\\\n5. Note any asset sizes/formats required from the User (e.g., neighborhood photo) and any technical hooks that Infrastructure/CMS teams must enable.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID DESIGN_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"D\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DESIGN_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-design###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Malformed Call Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis automated message is to inform you that you that one or more of your attached system calls was not in the correct format.\\\\n\\\\nThe system program can only accept calls in the correct format. Please correct your call(s) and resubmit.\\\\n\\\\nSee below for the specific errors generated by your calls.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nCall ID order-infra failed inspection: Call order-infra of type ORDER failed inspection: recipient agent ID NaN does not exist.\\\"\\n}\\n###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###order-infra###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Infrastructure & Deployment. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Select a low-cost, secure hosting approach suitable for ~100 WordPress users (e.g., reputable shared WP host or AWS Lightsail WP image) and compare at least two options with pricing, recommending one.\\\\n2. Detail exact setup steps: purchasing or linking the existing domain dunbaroakshoa.com, DNS changes, SSL (Let’s Encrypt or host-provided), automatic backups, and uptime monitoring—spell out every command or provider UI action deterministically.\\\\n3. Include WordPress installation steps, staging ↔ production workflow, and basic hardening (firewall, limited login attempts, automatic updates).\\\\n4. Provide estimated recurring and one-time costs, and note any free-tier limits.\\\\n5. Specify any dependencies or information you need from the CMS & Design directors.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID INFRA_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"4\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"INFRA_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-infra###\\n###order-cms###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for CMS Implementation. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Define the WordPress information architecture: Home, Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings (protected), News & Events (protected).\\\\n2. Recommend and justify specific free/low-cost plugins for: a) resident self-registration (~100 users) with admin approval code; b) content protection/membership; c) simple page builder or block pattern for non-technical updates; d) contact form; e) PDF file management.\\\\n3. Outline exact configuration steps for each plugin, user-role definitions, and sample workflow for the HOA admin to upload/update protected content and news posts without coding.\\\\n4. Address basic security (CAPTCHA, limited login attempts) and privacy (no unnecessary data collection).\\\\n5. List any settings or theme hooks the Design director must accommodate and any hosting prerequisites from Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"3\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-cms###\\n###order-design###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Design & Branding. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Propose a simple, professional visual identity: color palette (3–5 colors), typography (Google Fonts), and a logo concept appropriate for Dunbar Oaks HOA.\\\\n2. Select a free, responsive WordPress theme that supports the CMS director’s plugin choices; outline any child-theme or Customizer tweaks needed.\\\\n3. Provide step-by-step instructions for applying the branding in WordPress (logo upload, colors, fonts) and for customizing key page layouts (header, footer, navigation) without coding where possible.\\\\n4. Export a one-page style guide (PDF or image) for future reference.\\\\n5. Note any asset sizes/formats required from the User (e.g., neighborhood photo) and any technical hooks that Infrastructure/CMS teams must enable.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID DESIGN_PLAN_V1.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"2\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DESIGN_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-design###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:38:22.513Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-infra\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order INFRA_PLAN_V1 from agent 4: INFRASTRUCTURE & DEPLOYMENT – DETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP)\\\\\\\\nSequence ID: INFRA_PLAN_V1\\\\\\\\nResponsible Agent: Director-rank (Hearts)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nA. OPTION COMPARISON & RECOMMENDATION\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nOption 1 – AWS Lightsail WordPress Blueprint\\\\\\\\n  • Instance (Plan) – 1 vCPU / 1 GB RAM / 40 GB SSD\\\\\\\\n  • Price – $5.00 USD / month flat (first month free)  \\\\\\\\n  • Data transfer – 2 TB included; overage $0.09/GB  \\\\\\\\n  • Snapshot backup – manual or scheduled, $0.05 / GB-month (≈$2 / mo for 40 GB)\\\\\\\\n  • Integrated DNS zones (free for first 3 zones), bundled static IP, built-in HTTPS via Let’s Encrypt, and one-click scaling.\\\\\\\\n  • Root SSH & WP admin access, security groups (firewall) configurable, AWS CLI available for IaC.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nOption 2 – Namecheap “EasyWP Turbo” Managed WordPress\\\\\\\\n  • Price – $4.88 USD / mo (annual billing) or $8.88 / mo monthly  \\\\\\\\n  • Visitors – up to 200 k/month, 1.5 CPU & 768 MB RAM burstable  \\\\\\\\n  • Storage – 25 GB SSD  \\\\\\\\n  • Free CDN and SSL (Sectigo)  \\\\\\\\n  • Backups – daily automatic (free), on-demand $2.00 each  \\\\\\\\n  • Limited root / plugin control; no AWS-grade scalability.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRecommendation: AWS Lightsail WordPress Blueprint.\\\\\\\\n  – Similar pricing; stronger scalability path (upgrade instance or migrate to EC2/EKS), granular firewall rules, snapshot-level backups, CLI automation, and easier multi-environment cloning.  \\\\\\\\n  – Includes 1 static IP & free monthly cost credits for first month.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nB. HIGH-LEVEL DEPENDENCIES\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nD1. Registrar credentials for dunbaroakshoa.com (assumed currently at GoDaddy).  \\\\\\\\nD2. AWS root or IAM user with Lightsail + Route 53 + Certificate Manager permissions.  \\\\\\\\nD3. CMS/Design team to supply: (a) chosen WP theme & plugins list, (b) branding assets, (c) staging content requirements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nC. STEP-BY-STEP EXECUTION – FULLY DETERMINISTIC\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nNOTE: Steps are numbered; execute sequentially. Commands prefixed “$” are run from an authorized local shell with AWS CLI v2 configured (profile «do-hoa»). UI clicks use exact menu paths.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 0. Local Workstation Prep ——\\\\\\\\n0.1  Install AWS CLI v2 & Lightsailctl plugin (if not present):\\\\\\\\n     $ curl \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -o awscliv2.zip\\\\\\\\n     $ unzip awscliv2.zip && sudo ./aws/install\\\\\\\\n     $ pip install awscli-plugin-lightsail\\\\\\\\n0.2  Configure profile with least-privilege IAM creds:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws configure --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n     (enter Access Key, Secret, us-east-1, json)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 1. Networking & DNS ——\\\\\\\\n1.1  Create Route 53 public hosted zone (if DNS will migrate):\\\\\\\\n     $ aws route53 create-hosted-zone --name dunbaroakshoa.com --caller-reference $(date +%s) --profile do-hoa > /tmp/zone.json\\\\\\\\n     Record HostedZoneId = $(jq -r '.HostedZone.Id' /tmp/zone.json)\\\\\\\\n1.2  If keeping registrar DNS, skip 1.1 and obtain existing control panel.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 2. Lightsail Instance Provisioning ——\\\\\\\\n2.1  Allocate static IP:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail allocate-static-ip --static-ip-name do-prod-ip --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n2.2  Create production instance:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail create-instances \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --instance-names do-prod-wp \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --availability-zone us-east-1a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --blueprint-id wordpress \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --bundle-id micro_2_0 (represents 1GB/40GB) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --user-data file://disable_ping.sh \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n2.3  Attach static IP:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail attach-static-ip --static-ip-name do-prod-ip --instance-name do-prod-wp --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n2.4  Repeat 2.1-2.3 with names do-stage-ip / do-stage-wp for staging environment.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 3. DNS Records ——\\\\\\\\n3.1  Create A record \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"@\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" → static prod IP & CNAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"www\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" → dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\n     If Route 53:\\\\\\\\n     $ cat > /tmp/rr.json <<EOF\\\\\\\\n     {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Comment\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A + CNAME\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Changes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"UPSERT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecordSet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TTL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":300,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecords\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"<PROD_IP>\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"UPSERT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecordSet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"www.dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CNAME\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TTL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":300,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ResourceRecords\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]}}]}\\\\\\\\n     EOF\\\\\\\\n     $ aws route53 change-resource-record-sets --hosted-zone-id $HostedZoneId --change-batch file:///tmp/rr.json --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n3.2  At registrar, replace nameservers with those from Route 53 OR create A/CNAME records if staying.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 4. SSL/TLS Certificates ——\\\\\\\\n4.1  In Lightsail console → Networking → HTTPS → “Enable HTTPS” → Let’s Encrypt → pick dunbaroakshoa.com + www. System auto-installs certbot & cron renewals. Deterministic via CLI:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail create-certificate --certificate-name do-cert --domain-name dunbaroakshoa.com --subject-alternative-names www.dunbaroakshoa.com --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail attach-certificate-to-distribution ... (Lightsail auto-distribution optional)\\\\\\\\n4.2  Verify `https://dunbaroakshoa.com` green padlock in browser.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 5. WordPress Initialisation ——\\\\\\\\n5.1  Retrieve WP admin password:\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail get-instance --instance-name do-prod-wp --profile do-hoa | jq -r '.instance.username'\\\\\\\\n     ssh bitnami@<PROD_IP>\\\\\\\\n     $ cat ~/bitnami_application_password\\\\\\\\n5.2  Log into `https://dunbaroakshoa.com/wp-admin`, change password, set site title.\\\\\\\\n5.3  Install plugin “Limit Login Attempts Reloaded” (Security → Add New → search).\\\\\\\\n5.4  Enable automatic WP core/theme/plugin updates: Dashboard → Updates → “Enable automatic”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 6. Staging ↔ Production Workflow ——\\\\\\\\n6.1  Stage site lives on do-stage-wp, IP e.g., 3.3.3.3, DNS: staging.dunbaroakshoa.com (A record).\\\\\\\\n6.2  Deploy Pipeline (manual deterministic):\\\\\\\\n     a) WP Plugin “All-in-One WP Migration” installed on both envs.  \\\\\\\\n     b) On staging: Export → File.  \\\\\\\\n     c) scp file to local or directly import on production.  \\\\\\\\n     (Future: Implement Lightsail Snapshots & AWS CodePipeline for blue-green; out of scope but feasible.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 7. Backups ——\\\\\\\\n7.1  Automated snapshot schedule (daily, retain 7):\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail put-instance-public-ports --instance-name do-prod-wp --port-infos file://ports.json --profile do-hoa  # (allows snapshot API)\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail create-auto-snapshot-add-on --instance-name do-prod-wp --add-on-type AutoSnapshot --status Enabled --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n7.2  Confirm: $ aws lightsail get-auto-snapshots --instance-name do-prod-wp --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n7.3  Repeat for staging.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 8. Uptime Monitoring ——\\\\\\\\n8.1  Enable Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics (free for 100 canaries-runs per month in Free Tier):\\\\\\\\n     $ aws synthetics create-canary --name do-home-canary --code S3Bucket=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"synthetics-bucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",S3Key=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ping.zip\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --execution-role-arn <ROLE> --schedule \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rate(5 minutes)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --run-config timeoutInSeconds=60 --artifact-s3-location s3://synthetics-artifacts/ --runtime-version syn-nodejs-puppeteer-3.4 --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n8.2  Alarm: 2 consecutive failures triggers SNS → email admin.\\\\\\\\n     (Alternatively, use free UptimeRobot monitor if AWS budget sensitive.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 9. Firewall Hardening ——\\\\\\\\n9.1  Default Lightsail firewall: Allow 80/tcp, 443/tcp, 22/tcp (SSH) from owner IP only; disable ping.\\\\\\\\n     $ aws lightsail open-instance-public-ports --instance-name do-prod-wp --port-info fromPort=22,toPort=22,protocol=TCP,cidr=<OFFICE_IP>/32 --profile do-hoa\\\\\\\\n9.2  Disable XML-RPC: WP plugin “Disable XMLRPC-Pingback”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n—— 10. Post-Deployment Validation ——\\\\\\\\n10.1  SSL Labs test score ≥ A.  \\\\\\\\n10.2  Wordfence scan passes; login attempts limited.  \\\\\\\\n10.3  CloudWatch canary status OK.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nD. COST SUMMARY (USD)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nRECURRING\\\\\\\\n  • Lightsail Prod instance: $5.00 / mo\\\\\\\\n  • Lightsail Stage instance: $5.00 / mo (can be stopped when idle to <$1)\\\\\\\\n  • Snapshots (~40 GB each): 2 × $2.00 ≈ $4.00 / mo\\\\\\\\n  • Route 53 Hosted Zone: $0.50 / mo + $0.40 / million queries (negligible)\\\\\\\\n  • CloudWatch Canaries: <$1 in Free Tier (first year) ⇒ then $4.50 / mo if 5-min interval\\\\\\\\nTotal steady-state ≈ $14.50 – $18.00 / month\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nONE-TIME\\\\\\\\n  • Domain transfer (if moving registrars): ~$9.00 (includes 1-year renewal)  \\\\\\\\n  • Initial snapshot storage grows linearly but negligible (<$1) first month\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFREE-TIER / NO-COST ITEMS\\\\\\\\n  • First Lightsail month free  \\\\\\\\n  • Let’s Encrypt SSL  \\\\\\\\n  • Up to 3 Route 53 DNS health checks free for 12 months  \\\\\\\\n  • AWS Free Tier 1 GB snapshot storage  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nE. HAND-OFF ARTIFACTS\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nE1. Generated HostedZoneId and static IPs – to be documented in shared secrets vault.\\\\\\\\nE2. Saved AWS CLI commands log (/var/log/infra-deploy-$(date).log) for audit.\\\\\\\\nE3. CloudFormation template (optional) to codify steps 2-7 – can be produced on request.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nF. NEXT-STE P REQUESTS TO CMS / DESIGN DIRECTORS\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nF1. Confirm choice of theme/plugins so we can pre-install in AMI snapshot.  \\\\\\\\nF2. Supply favicon & logo to complete staging site before production push.  \\\\\\\\nF3. Provide colour palette to configure CDN edge rules for image optimisation (optional).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nEnd of DEP – ready for Partagaz D review.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-cms\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order CMS_PLAN_V1 from agent 3: **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – CMS_PLAN_V1**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nA. HOSTING & BASELINE\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Hosting prerequisites (Infrastructure team)\\\\\\\\n   a. PHP ≥ 8.1, memory_limit ≥ 256 M, max_upload_filesize ≥ 32 M.\\\\\\\\n   b. MariaDB 10.5 / MySQL 8.0, InnoDB default.\\\\\\\\n   c. HTTPS enabled (Let’s Encrypt or other TLS cert) before public launch.\\\\\\\\n   d. Cron jobs allowed (for WP‐Cron replacement if traffic < 1k/day this can stay virtual).\\\\\\\\n   e. SMTP credentials or transactional-mail service (Postmark / SendGrid free tier) for registration emails.\\\\\\\\n   f. File-system write permissions for wp-content and install zip uploads.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Fresh WordPress 6.5.x install in root directory; enforce automatic minor/major core updates:\\\\\\\\n   wp-config.php →\\\\\\\\n   define('WP_AUTO_UPDATE_CORE','minor');\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Theme baseline picked by Design director: “Twenty Twenty-Four” **or** “Astra Free”.\\\\\\\\n   • Must support: full-site-editing (FSE) hooks `header`, `footer`, `sidebar` if Astra.\\\\\\\\n   • Keep child-theme blank (style.css, functions.php) reserved for any CSS/JS overrides but *initially empty* to keep DEP deterministic.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nB. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE (IA)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nCreate pages in this exact slug order:\\\\\\\\n1. `/`  → “Home”\\\\\\\\n2. `/contact-us/` → “Contact Us”\\\\\\\\n3. `/bylaws/` → “HOA Bylaws” (public)\\\\\\\\n4. `/schools/` → “Nearby Schools” (public)\\\\\\\\n5. `/dues/` → “Dues” (PROTECTED)\\\\\\\\n6. `/annual-meetings/` → “Annual Meetings” (PROTECTED)\\\\\\\\n7. `/news-events/` → “News & Events” (PROTECTED)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNavigation menu “Main Menu” created and assigned to Theme primary location using identical order.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nC. PLUGIN STACK (all free unless noted)\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. User self-registration + manual admin approval + access-code field\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“User Registration – Custom Registration Form, Login and User Profile”** by WP Everest.\\\\\\\\n     – Free tier supports manual approval, custom fields & form shortcodes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Content/membership protection\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Content Control – User Access Restriction”** by Code Atlantic (100 % free, no paywall).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Simple page/block builder for non-technical updates\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Kadence Blocks – Gutenberg Blocks for Page Builder Features”** (free) – adds pre-made block patterns, accordions, tabs; stays inside core editor.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Contact form with CAPTCHA\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“WPForms Lite”** (free) – includes hCaptcha & reCAPTCHA v2/v3 support.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. PDF file management / embed & protection\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“EmbedPress”** (free) – Gutenberg block to embed PDF inline.\\\\\\\\n   • **“Prevent Direct Access – PDA Lite”** (free) – protects PDFs so file URLs respect membership rules.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Security hardening\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Limit Login Attempts Reloaded”** (free).\\\\\\\\n   • (Optional) “WP 2FA” free module if MFA desired later.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Role/Capability management convenience\\\\\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Members”** by MemberPress (free) – create Custom Role “Resident”.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nD. STEP-BY-STEP CONFIGURATION\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nD1. Global order of operations (deterministic):\\\\\\\\n   1. Complete WP install (A2).\\\\\\\\n   2. Install theme (A3).\\\\\\\\n   3. Install *all* plugins in section C but keep them **deactivated**.\\\\\\\\n   4. Activate plugins sequentially in this exact order to avoid capability conflicts:\\\\\\\\n      a. Members\\\\\\\\n      b. User Registration\\\\\\\\n      c. Content Control\\\\\\\\n      d. Kadence Blocks\\\\\\\\n      e. WPForms Lite\\\\\\\\n      f. EmbedPress\\\\\\\\n      g. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite\\\\\\\\n      h. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\\\\\n   5. Create roles, forms, rules as below.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD2. Members plugin – role definitions\\\\\\\\n   • Create custom role **Resident**.\\\\\\\\n     Capabilities: `read`, `edit_posts` = false, `upload_files` = false. (Leave all others unchecked.)\\\\\\\\n   • (Core) Keep Administrator, Editor defaults.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD3. User Registration plugin – registration form\\\\\\\\n   1. Create new form “Resident Signup”.\\\\\\\\n   2. Add core fields: First Name, Last Name, Email (username), Password.\\\\\\\\n   3. Add custom Text field “Access Code”.\\\\\\\\n      – Field meta-key: `hoa_access_code`.\\\\\\\\n      – Field set as *required*.\\\\\\\\n   4. Enable *Manual Admin Approval* (Settings ▸ General ▸ User Login Option ▸ “Admin Approve”).\\\\\\\\n   5. Form setting ▸ *Enable email confirmation* = OFF (because approval already required).\\\\\\\\n   6. Place validation rule via form *Field Visibility & Logic*:\\\\\\\\n      – If `hoa_access_code` ≠ “NEIGHBOR2024” (example), display error “Invalid HOA code”.\\\\\\\\n   7. Save form; copy generated shortcode `[user_registration_form id=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"XX\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]`.\\\\\\\\n   8. Create WordPress page `/register/` titled “Resident Registration”, paste shortcode.\\\\\\\\n   9. In WP ▸ Settings ▸ General ▸ “Membership – Anyone can register” = **unchecked** (security).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD4. Content Control – protection rules\\\\\\\\n   • Rule 1: Protect Pages `Dues`, `Annual Meetings`, `News & Events`.\\\\\\\\n     – Access condition: Logged-in users with role = Resident OR ≥ Editor.\\\\\\\\n     – Redirect on failure: `/register/` (or custom message page).\\\\\\\\n   • Rule 2: Protect Media Files category “Protected PDFs” (auto-created by PDA Lite) with same role condition.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD5. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite – PDF handling\\\\\\\\n   1. Settings ▸ Permalink Type: “Encrypted URL” (default).\\\\\\\\n   2. Upload PDF → Media Library → toggle “Protect this file”.\\\\\\\\n   3. Copy shortcode `[pda_protected url=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" download=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]` and insert inside protected pages.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD6. WPForms Lite – contact form\\\\\\\\n   1. Create form “HOA Contact”. Fields: Name, Email, Message.\\\\\\\\n   2. Settings ▸ Spam Protection → enable Google reCAPTCHA v3 (site key provided separately by Infrastructure).\\\\\\\\n   3. Notifications → send to `hoaboard@example.com`.\\\\\\\\n   4. Embed form in “Contact Us” page using Gutenberg block.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD7. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\\\\\n   • Settings → Lockout at 4 retries, 30 min lockout, 24 h increase, GDPR consent banner OFF.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD8. Kadence Blocks (non-technical editing enablement)\\\\\\\\n   • Install Starter Templates if Astra theme chosen; else use built-in patterns.\\\\\\\\n   • Provide training doc (outside DEP) listing: Accordion (meeting minutes), Info Box (dues summary), Gallery (events photos).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nE. SAMPLE WORKFLOWS\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Resident onboarding\\\\\\\\n   a. User visits /register/; enters data + HOA access code.\\\\\\\\n   b. Admin receives email “User Registration Requires Approval”.\\\\\\\\n   c. Admin logs in → User Registration ▸ Users → Approve.\\\\\\\\n   d. User receives “Your account is approved” email, logs in, sees protected menu items.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. HOA Admin uploads protected PDF (e.g., Annual Meeting Minutes)\\\\\\\\n   a. Media ▸ Add New → upload PDF → click “Protect this file”.\\\\\\\\n   b. Copy auto-generated shortcode.\\\\\\\\n   c. Edit “Annual Meetings” page (block editor) → add ‘Shortcode’ block → paste.\\\\\\\\n   d. Click Update; file now downloadable only by Residents.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Post News item\\\\\\\\n   a. Posts ▸ Add New → title + content; set Category = “Members Only News”.\\\\\\\\n   b. Content Control rule can also blanket-protect this category if preferred (create Rule 3 referencing category).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nF. SECURITY / PRIVACY CHECKLIST\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n✔ SSL mandatory.\\\\\\\\n✔ Limit Login Attempts active.\\\\\\\\n✔ reCAPTCHA on Contact form.\\\\\\\\n✔ Manual approval prevents spam users.\\\\\\\\n✔ Only essential PII collected (name, email, HOA access code). No DOB, phone, etc.\\\\\\\\n✔ Weekly automated backups via host or UpdraftPlus (free) – schedule to external storage (Google Drive free tier).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nG. DESIGN TEAM HOOKS & NOTES\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Theme must output `wp_nav_menu()` location “primary”.\\\\\\\\n2. Register sidebar “Protected Sidebar” (optional) if theme offers sidebars → may hold quick-links visible only to Residents via `is_user_logged_in()`.\\\\\\\\n3. Ensure CSS for `.pda-protected` shortcode wrapper inherits theme typography.\\\\\\\\n4. If using Astra, keep header builder; add custom menu item CSS class `menu-item-protected` (style to match but hide via `display:none` unauth if plugin flashes). Not needed for FSE theme.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nH. DELIVERABLE SUMMARY\\\\\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• Working WordPress site with defined IA, plugins configured, roles created.\\\\\\\\n• No paid licenses required; all plugins on WP.org repo.\\\\\\\\n• Non-technical HOA admins can manage protected documents and news via Gutenberg + Kadence Blocks.\\\\\\\\n• Security hardening & privacy minimal compliance done.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-design\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order DESIGN_PLAN_V1 from agent 2: **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – Design & Branding for Dunbar Oaks HOA**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nA. OBJECTIVE\\\\\\\\nCreate a simple, professional visual identity and apply it to a free, responsive WordPress site, then export a one-page style guide. All steps are deterministic and can be executed in sequence by any Administrator with WP back-end access (no code-level edits unless explicitly noted as *optional*).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nB. PRE-REQUISITES & DEPENDENCIES\\\\\\\\n1. WordPress ≥ 6.4 installed, user has Administrator role.\\\\\\\\n2. Required free plugins pre-installed but **not yet configured**:\\\\\\\\n   • Elementor (page builder)  \\\\\\\\n   • Elementor Header & Footer Builder OR Astra Widgets (optional)  \\\\\\\\n   • Customizer Export/Import  \\\\\\\\n   • SVG Support (for vector logo upload)\\\\\\\\n3. “Customizer > Additional CSS” panel remains enabled (default).\\\\\\\\n4. User can upload media ≤ 5 MB per file.\\\\\\\\n5. Infrastructure team whitelisted fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com (needed to load Google Fonts).\\\\\\\\n6. Assets to be collected from User before Step E-1 (see Section G).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nC. VISUAL IDENTITY SPECIFICATION\\\\\\\\n1. Color Palette (accessible contrast, WCAG AA):\\\\\\\\n   • PRIMARY – “Oak Green”   #356859  (rgb 53 ,104 , 89)   \\\\\\\\n   • SECONDARY – “Stone Sand” #E3B23C (rgb 227,178, 60)   \\\\\\\\n   • ACCENT – “Deep Teal”    #37967F (rgb 55 ,150 ,127)   \\\\\\\\n   • LIGHT NEUTRAL – “Linen” #F6F5F3 (rgb 246,245,243)   \\\\\\\\n   • DARK NEUTRAL – “Charcoal” #2F2F2F (rgb 47 , 47 , 47)\\\\\\\\n2. Typography (Google Fonts, free-to-use):\\\\\\\\n   • Headings (H1–H4) – \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Poppins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", weight 600  \\\\\\\\n   • Body / UI – \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Open Sans\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", weight 400/600  \\\\\\\\n   • Backup stack: “Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif”.\\\\\\\\n3. Logo Concept (to be produced/manually designed outside DEP):\\\\\\\\n   A minimal, flat oak-tree silhouette encircled by a thin ring; to the right, stacked text “Dunbar Oaks” (bold) above smaller “HOA” (regular). Single-color Oak Green on transparent background.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nD. THEME SELECTION & SET-UP\\\\\\\\nSTEP D-1  Install & Activate Theme\\\\\\\\n   • Navigate Appearance > Themes > Add New.  \\\\\\\\n   • Search “Astra”.  \\\\\\\\n   • Click Install → Activate.\\\\\\\\nSTEP D-2  Generate Child Theme (zero-code)\\\\\\\\n   • Visit https://wpastra.com/child-theme-generator/.  \\\\\\\\n   • Enter site name; download ZIP; upload via Appearance > Themes > Add New > Upload; Activate child theme.  \\\\\\\\n   (Keeps future CSS overrides isolated; no further edits required.)\\\\\\\\nSTEP D-3  Confirm responsive breakpoints (Astra default: 921 px tablet, 544 px mobile) – suits requirement; no change needed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nE. APPLY BRANDING (no-code unless flagged *)\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-1  Upload Logo/Favicon\\\\\\\\n   • Go to Appearance > Customize > Site Identity.  \\\\\\\\n   • Upload *logo.svg* (preferred) **512 × 512 px** or *logo.png* on transparent background.  \\\\\\\\n   • Set “Site Title” = blank (logo includes text).  \\\\\\\\n   • Upload *Site Icon* 512 × 512 px PNG.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-2  Set Global Colors\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Global > Colors.  \\\\\\\\n   • Base Color → PRIMARY (#356859).  \\\\\\\\n   • Link / Accent Color → ACCENT (#37967F).  \\\\\\\\n   • Heading Text → PRIMARY.  \\\\\\\\n   • Body Text → DARK NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Background → LIGHT NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-3  Configure Global Typography\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Global > Typography.  \\\\\\\\n   • Font Family –\\\\\\\\n       Headings: Poppins, 600.  \\\\\\\\n       Base: Open Sans, 400.  \\\\\\\\n   • Font Sizes (desktop): H1 = 42 px, H2 = 32 px, Base = 18 px.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.  \\\\\\\\n   *Optional code‐free*: If Astra’s built-in Google Fonts list lacks weights, install “Astra Custom Fonts” plugin.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-4  Build Header\\\\\\\\n   • Appearance > Astra Header Builder.  \\\\\\\\n   • Drag “Site Logo” left, “Primary Menu” center, “Button” (label “Pay Dues”) right with link to payment portal.  \\\\\\\\n   • Mobile – enable Off-Canvas Menu.  \\\\\\\\n   • Background Color → LIGHT NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Border bottom 2 px PRIMARY.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-5  Build Footer\\\\\\\\n   • Footer Builder → four-column layout.\\\\\\\\n       Col 1: Logo (50 px height).  \\\\\\\\n       Col 2: Quick Links menu.  \\\\\\\\n       Col 3: Address & contact (text).  \\\\\\\\n       Col 4: Social icons.  \\\\\\\\n   • Background color PRIMARY, text LIGHT NEUTRAL.  \\\\\\\\n   • Save.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-6  Navigation Styling\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Header > Primary Menu.  \\\\\\\\n   • Font: Poppins 600, size 16 px.  \\\\\\\\n   • Link hover color ACCENT.  \\\\\\\\n   • Active item underline 3 px ACCENT.\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-7  Page Layout Defaults\\\\\\\\n   • Customize > Global > Container.  \\\\\\\\n   • Width 1200 px; Inside Padding 2 rem.  \\\\\\\\n   • Blog Archive Layout: Grid 2 columns.  \\\\\\\\n   • Disable sidebar globally (can enable per-page later).\\\\\\\\nSTEP E-8  Import/Export Customizer Settings\\\\\\\\n   • Tools > Import/Export Customizer.  \\\\\\\\n   • Click “Export” → downloads .dat file (store for disaster recovery).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nF. ONE-PAGE STYLE-GUIDE EXPORT\\\\\\\\nSTEP F-1  Create Private Page\\\\\\\\n   • Pages > Add New → Title “Brand Style Guide”.  \\\\\\\\n   • Visibility: Private.  \\\\\\\\n   • Edit with Elementor.\\\\\\\\nSTEP F-2  Build Sections\\\\\\\\n   1. Hero heading “Dunbar Oaks HOA – Brand Guide” (H1).  \\\\\\\\n   2. Color Swatches: five columns (use “Inner Section”). For each color: 100 × 100 px box → background respective hex; below, text label & hex code.  \\\\\\\\n   3. Typography: two columns – left headings (H1–H4) sample text; right body paragraph sample.  \\\\\\\\n   4. Logo Usage: insert full-color logo (200 px), plus “Do/Don’t” list.  \\\\\\\\n   5. Iconography / Buttons: show primary button (Oak Green bg, light text) & link styling.\\\\\\\\nSTEP F-3  Export as PDF/Image\\\\\\\\n   • Elementor → icon ▸ Print to PDF ▸ “Save as PDF” A4 portrait.